{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236225": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Assistant/Associate/Professor",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Open Rank - Assistant/Associate/Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Open Rank - Assistant/Associate/Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), research statement, teaching statement, and contact information for three professional references. Application review will begin on December 1, 2026. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194966EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Open Rank - Assistant/Associate/Professor Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with experience and education Work Schedule Monday - Friday Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering About the Department The Department of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering ( MAE ) at North Carolina State University (Raleigh, NC) is the largest in the state and among the largest and most prominent in the nation. The department offers Bachelor of Science (BS), Master of Science (MS) and Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) degrees in both Mechanical Engineering (ME) and Aerospace Engineering (AE). The department also offers accelerated BS/MS degrees in both programs. Current research specialization in MAE includes dynamic systems and controls, robotics and automation, biomechanics, design optimization, smart materials and structures, MEMS and NEMS , advanced manufacturing, renewable energy systems, combustion, aerodynamics, UAV flight research, hypersonics, propulsion, space exploration systems, and computational fluid dynamics. The MAE Department has an enrollment of over 1,800 undergraduates and 400 graduate students. The department is housed in Engineering Building III , a four-story, 250,000-square foot facility built in 2010. Several additional facilities house wind tunnels, an anechoic chamber, internal combustion engine dynamometers, and additional research labs. NC State’s location on Centennial Campus, combined with its proximity to the Research Triangle Park and neighboring universities, provides extensive opportunities for academic and industrial interaction and collaboration. The mission of the MAE department is to be a flagship engineering department that benefits all people of North Carolina and the global society by making a profound impact on current and emerging science and technologies; fostering exemplary, synergistic multidisciplinary research and education programs in close partnership with industry and government; providing the environment for innovative professional and scholarly development; and graduating highly skilled, ethical engineers who will thrive in a rapidly changing world and be future leaders in technology and society. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering at North Carolina State University invites applications for multiple tenured or tenure track faculty positions at the rank of Assistant/Associate/Full Professor with particular interest in aerostructures, manufacturing, and engineering design disciplines. Aerostructures: Including but not limited to: 1) structures for space platforms; 2) fluid and/or thermal structure interactions, aerothermoelasticity, nonlinear structural dynamics and multiphysics phenomena as it relates to aerostructures; 3) physical reservoir computing and concepts relating to mechanically embodied intelligence for aerospace applications; and 4) advanced multifunctional structures for aerospace applications. Advanced Manufacturing for aerospace, mechanical, and marine applications: Including but not limited to: 1) modeling and simulations of manufacturing processes for innovation and scale up; 2) rapid and advanced manufacturing of hot structures and extreme-environment components, including space manufacturing; 3) multiphysics modeling, sensing, and process monitoring to inform manufacturing decisions; 4) AI/ML-enabled, intelligent, and autonomous manufacturing, including digital twins and advanced process control; and 5) quantum manufacturing paradigms, including quantum-enabled manufacturing and other transformative manufacturing technologies. Complex System Design for aerospace, mechanical, and marine applications, exploring how advanced computational tools can change the way systems are conceived, optimized, and manufactured . Including but not limited to: 1) Human-AI collaboration and co-teaming; 2) multidisciplinary optimization tools to synchronize design and digital manufacturing; 3) design decision-making under uncertainty; and 4) the strategic management of change to create resilient systems. Other Responsibilities Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, or a related field, completed before the start date. Demonstrated excellence in teaching both undergraduate and graduate courses. Other Required Qualifications n/a Preferred Qualifications Applicants with expertise in applications of aerostructures, manufacturing, and engineering design disciplines. Required License(s) or Certification(s) n/a Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 10/14/2026 Anticipated Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), research statement, teaching statement, and contact information for three professional references. Application review will begin on December 1, 2026. Position Details Position Number 00000648 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 140901 - Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? (Open Ended Question) If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for References Research Statement Teaching Statement Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236182": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant/Associate Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant/Associate Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications require the submission of an application, cover letter, CV, and contact information for three professional references. Confidential references will be contacted only for those candidates moving forward in the process. A cover letter should clearly state the applicant's interest in North Carolina State University as well as research and teaching interests. Please address any additional inquiries to: Dr. Tom Zagenczyk, Professor, Department of Management, Innovation, and Entrepreneurship Poole College of Management North Carolina State University Campus Box 7229 Raleigh, NC 27695 tzagenc@ncsu.edu Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194968EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with experience. Work Schedule Monday - Friday; evenings and some weekends may be required. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Management, Innovation & Entrepreneurship About the Department The Poole College of Management actively engages with industry and academia to create an innovative and collaborative intellectual environment that fosters learning, scholarship, and service. We’re deeply rooted in NC State’s history as a university that excels at science, technology, engineering, and math. Our college’s varied student body — over 4,000 students — hails from across North Carolina, the United States, and the world. Our faculty are thought leaders and field-tested experts with enduring ties to the world of business. Poole College of Management has six academic departments: Accounting, Economics, Finance, Information Technology Analytics and Operations ( ITAO ), Marketing, and Management, Innovation and Entrepreneurship ( MIE ). We offer bachelor’s degrees in accounting, business administration, and economics; master’s degrees in accounting, business administration ( MBA ), economics, and management (including specialized degrees); as well as joint doctoral degrees in economics and operations research. Among our non-degree programs, we offer Executive Education and graduate certificates. The college houses several initiatives fostering research, learning, and corporate engagement: Enterprise Risk Management Initiative, Entrepreneurship Clinic, and Supply Chain Resource Cooperative. The college is fully accredited by the AACSB . To learn more about our College, visit: https://poole.ncsu.edu The MIE Department embodies excellence in research, teaching, and industry engagement. Interdisciplinary in nature, the MIE department is a diverse and highly collegial group of scholars whose research focuses on organizational behavior, human resource management, leadership, strategy, and entrepreneurship. MIE faculty conduct high-quality impactful research published in premiere and FT-50 journals such as AMR , AMJ , SMJ , SEJ , JAP , JOM , Organization Science, Management Science, OBHDP , JBV , ETP , JMS , and HBR . Faculty hold or have held roles as Associate Editor/Editor in Chief for such journals as AMR , AMJ , GOM , JBV , and ETP . The department contributes to the BSBA degree, the MBA degree, and executive education. To learn more about MIE , visit: https://poole.ncsu.edu/mie/about Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Management, Innovation, and Entrepreneurship ( MIE ) in the Poole College of Management at North Carolina State University invites applications for a tenure-track, open-rank Assistant or Associate Professor in Organizational Behavior or Strategic Human Resource Management , with an anticipated start date of August 2027. Position Responsibilities The successful candidate will be expected to: Develop and maintain a high-quality, impactful research program resulting in publications in leading peer-reviewed journals. Deliver high-quality instruction in Organizational Behavior, Strategic Human Resource Management, and/or related areas at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Contribute to the academic mission of the department, college, and university through service and professional engagement. Collaborate effectively with faculty and contribute to a collegial, intellectually engaging, and interdisciplinary academic environment. Engage with students, faculty, and other stakeholders in ways that advance the teaching, research, and service missions of the department. Candidates should demonstrate a strong record of, or clear potential for, scholarly excellence in Organizational Behavior, Strategic Human Resource Management, or closely related areas. Candidates considered at the Associate Professor level should have an established record of high-quality scholarship, effective teaching, and academic or professional service commensurate with rank. This position offers an opportunity to join an engaged academic community within the MIE Department and Poole College of Management, advance impactful research, and contribute to the education and development of future business leaders. Faculty rank and compensation will be determined based on the successful candidate’s qualifications, experience, and scholarly record. Other Responsibilities Contributing member of the department, college, and university. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience An earned Ph.D. in a relevant area is required. Other Required Qualifications Qualified candidates should possess a strong record in research, teaching, and service, or have the potential to achieve the same. For consideration, candidates should demonstrate strong scholarly research capabilities consistent with a Research 1 university and an ability to teach at undergraduate and graduate levels. Perform other duties as assigned by the department head. Candidates must be a contributing faculty member to department and college service activities. Preferred Qualifications Preferred candidates will: Thrive in an interdisciplinary environment Conduct research and teach courses that span levels of analysis Navigate between research and practice in alignment with our “Think and Do” motto Have experience in submitting and/or obtaining research grants Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 10/14/2026 Anticipated Close Date 11/11/2026; if posting is still active we are accepting and reviewing applications. Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications require the submission of an application, cover letter, CV, and contact information for three professional references. Confidential references will be contacted only for those candidates moving forward in the process. A cover letter should clearly state the applicant’s interest in North Carolina State University as well as research and teaching interests. Please address any additional inquiries to: Dr. Tom Zagenczyk, Professor, Department of Management, Innovation, and Entrepreneurship Poole College of Management North Carolina State University Campus Box 7229 Raleigh, NC 27695 tzagenc@ncsu.edu Position Details Position Number 00112388 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 204001 - Management, Innovation & Entrepreneurship EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236164": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Scholar",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In addition to your application please submit a cover letter, resume, and the contact information for at least three professional references. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191789PD Position Number 00112398 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 141101 - Nuclear Engineering Department 141101 - Nuclear Engineering Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties The FPAC LAB at North Carolina State University is seeking an early-career scientist to lead impurity powder injection for wall conditioning experiments and to develop a model-based controller for the impurity powder dropper ( IPD ) on the KSTAR tokamak. The position is part of the multi-institutional DOE Office of Science FES project that is led by Princeton Plasma Physics Laboratory. As fusion devices transition to tungsten walls, real-time injection of low-Z powders offers a route to continuous wall conditioning without extended downtimes. The NC State scope is to deploy the IPD to integrate wall conditioning into high-performance plasma scenarios at KSTAR while minimizing the amount of injected impurity material. The successful candidate will complete the IPD feedback control loop and develop an AI-/model-based predictive controller for injection rates that can be transferred to future devices, and design control schemes for long-pulse real-time wall conditioning. The role involves close, sustained collaboration with the KSTAR team and with U.S. collaborators, including travel to Korea for experimental campaigns. The position is under the supervision of Dr. Florian Laggner and will be based at the Department of Nuclear Engineering in Raleigh, NC. Duties and Responsibilities include: Develop and deploy a real-time, model-based controller for impurity powder injection on the KSTAR tokamak. Design and test control schemes for real-time wall conditioning in long-pulse scenarios that minimize the injected material while maintaining compatibility with high performance plasma operation. Develop a predictive, AI-/machine-learning-based model of IPD injection rates and powder delivery, suitable for real-time control. Complete the IPD feedback control loop and integrate it with the KSTAR plasma control system. Plan, execute and analyze experiments at KSTAR . Prepare and run experiments during international campaigns. Coordinate technical work with collaborators at PPPL and the KSTAR team. Communicate research results. Create scientific peer-reviewed publications. Attend conferences with oral and poster presentations. Provide research progress reports. Mentor undergraduate and graduate students at NC State. Provide scientific direction, guidance and mentorship to students as a key member of the FPAC LAB . Other Work/Responsibilities Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8am - 5pm, and off-hours as needed, including off-hours to support experiments in the KSTAR time zone. Flexible work arrangements are possible; domestic and international travel as needed for collaborative research, experimental campaigns Department Required Skills n/a Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Ability to function well in a fast-paced research environment, set priorities to accomplish multiple tasks within deadlines and move rapidly from one task area to another. Strong interpersonal skills and ability to communicate effectively with a diverse, international project team at various career stages. Ability to adapt to ever-changing needs, adjust or extend working hours, and travel internationally as required. An ideal candidate will have one or more of the following qualifications. Familiarity with wall conditioning, impurity or powder injection, and plasma-material interactions. Experience with real-time control systems, feedback algorithms, or a tokamak plasma control system. Experience applying machine learning or data-driven surrogate modeling to physical or engineering systems. Prior experience working within an international, multi- institutional research collaboration. Required License or Certification n/a Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $85,000 - $90,000 per year depending on experience If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 10/13/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236163 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? (Open Ended Question) If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Contact Information for References Resume/CV Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236149": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In addition to your application, please submit the following: 1. Curriculum Vitae 2. Cover Letter 3. Research Statement 4. Teaching Statement Review of applications will begin 11/1/2026. Please direct any questions about this position to statistics-jobs@ncsu.edu. Additionally, please have three letters of recommendation sent directly to statistics-jobs@ncsu.edu . The start date for both positions is August 2027. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194937EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant Professor Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with education and experience Work Schedule Core Business Hours: Monday - Friday; 8:00 AM - 5:00 PM; hours will vary based on teaching schedule and research needs. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Statistics About the Department The Department of Statistics at North Carolina State University was founded in 1941 by Gertrude M. Cox and is one of the oldest and largest statistics programs in the country. The primary function of the Department is to achieve outstanding research, teaching, mentoring, consulting and collaborations on campus and world-wide, within a cohesive department, where all students, faculty, and staff receive fair treatment. The Department has approximately 40 faculty members, along with more than 260 undergraduate and 150 graduate students. We are the “birthplace” of SAS Institute, the world’s largest privately-owned software company, and one which specializes in statistical applications. The Department maintains a close relationship with SAS and other industry partners through student programs and activities. The Department has expertise in a number of research areas (see https://statistics.sciences.ncsu.edu/research/research-areas/ ). Our graduate program, which is the top producer of statistics PhDs, is nationally recognized for graduate education and research, ranking #18 nationally in US News and World Reports (see https://statistics.sciences.ncsu.edu/know-us/rankings-awards-stats/ ); we also have a thriving online master’s program with approximately 100 students. NC State promotes an integrated approach to problem solving that transforms lives and provides leadership for social, economic, and technological development across North Carolina and around the world. NC State’s land grant mission of teaching, research and service is dedicated to the service of North Carolina and its people. Applicants are encouraged to review the institution’s mission, vision and strategic plan, and consider how their background, interest and experience would enable them to support the university. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Statistics at North Carolina State University in Raleigh, North Carolina, invites applications for two 9-month tenure-track Assistant Professor positions, each with a distinct research focus: Climate and environmental statistics, including sustainability. Statistics in human health and health sciences, including biostatistics and bioinformatics. For both positions, we are particularly interested in scholars whose research advances statistical approaches to complex challenges in their respective areas and may intersect with emerging fields such as machine learning and artificial intelligence. Key Responsibilities: Develop and sustain an independent, externally funded research program that advances statistical methodology and applications in the relevant research area. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in statistics and related fields, and mentor doctoral students in research, dissertation development, and completion. Collaborate across disciplines to address complex scientific challenges through statistical and data science approaches, while contributing to the department’s academic mission and professional and university service. Other Responsibilities n/a Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Ph.D. in Statistics, Biostatistics, Data Science, or related field by the time of employment. Other Required Qualifications Research expertise in statistics or a related field, with relevance to the designated application area. Potential to develop a sustained research program and contribute to peer-reviewed scholarship. Ability to teach statistics effectively. Preferred Qualifications n/a Required License(s) or Certification(s) n/a Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 10/09/2026 Anticipated Close Date 12/1/2026; if posting is still active we are still accepting and reviewing applications Special Instructions to Applicants In addition to your application, please submit the following: 1. Curriculum Vitae 2. Cover Letter 3. Research Statement 4. Teaching Statement Review of applications will begin 11/1/2026. Please direct any questions about this position to statistics-jobs@ncsu.edu. Additionally, please have three letters of recommendation sent directly to statistics-jobs@ncsu.edu . The start date for both positions is August 2027. Position Details Position Number 00112363 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 178501 - Statistics EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Research Statement Teaching Statement Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
