    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236123": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Accounting",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant Professor, Accounting Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant Professor, Accounting Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include the following as part of your application materials: 1. Cover Letter 2. Resume/CV 3. Contact information for at least three professional references. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194949EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant Professor, Accounting Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with education and experience. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00 am - 5:00 pm (weekends and nights as needed) Job Location Raleigh, North Carolina Department Accounting - Poole College of Management About the Department The Poole College of Management actively engages with industry and academia to create an innovative and collaborative intellectual environment that fosters learning, scholarship, and service. We’re deeply rooted in NC State’s history as a university that excels at science, technology, engineering, and math. Our college’s varied student body — over 4,000 students — hails from across North Carolina, the United States, and the world. Our faculty are thought leaders and field-tested experts with enduring ties to the world of business. Poole College of Management has six academic departments: Accounting, Economics, Finance, Information Technology Analytics and Operations ( ITAO ), Marketing, Management, Innovation, and Entrepreneurship ( MIE ). We offer bachelor’s degrees in accounting, business administration, and economics; master’s degrees in accounting, business administration ( MBA ), economics, and management (including specialized degrees); as well as joint doctoral degrees in economics and operations research. Among our non-degree programs, we offer Executive Education and graduate certificates. The college houses three initiatives fostering research, learning, and corporate engagement. Faculty in the Department of Accounting lead the Enterprise Risk Management Initiative, which works closely with executives and boards in helping them identify and manage risks important to their strategic success. Poole College and the Department of Accounting are fully accredited by the AACSB . To learn more about our College, visit: https://poole.ncsu.edu Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Accounting in the Poole College of Management at North Carolina State University invites applications for a 9-month tenure-track Assistant Professor of Accounting , with an anticipated start date of August 2027 . The department welcomes applications from both emerging scholars entering their first faculty appointment and experienced Assistant Professors. Key Responsibilities: Develop and maintain a high-quality, impactful research program in accounting resulting in publications in leading peer-reviewed journals and consistent with the expectations of an R1 research university. Deliver high-quality instruction in accounting at the undergraduate and graduate levels, including the Master of Accounting ( MAC ) and MBA programs. Contribute to teaching needs in areas such as managerial accounting, auditing, accounting information systems, analytics, artificial intelligence, and related areas. Contribute to the academic mission of the department, college, and university through service and professional engagement. Collaborate effectively with faculty and contribute to a collegial, intellectually engaging, and interdisciplinary academic environment. Engage with students, faculty, and other stakeholders in ways that advance the teaching, research, and service missions of the department. If you are looking for an opportunity to join an engaged academic community within the Department of Accounting and Poole College of Management, advance impactful accounting research, and contribute to the education and development of future accounting and business professionals, we encourage to you apply. Compensation will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s qualifications, experience, and scholarly record. Other Responsibilities Perform other duties as assigned by the department head. Candidates must be a contributing faculty member to department and college service activities. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Ph.D., or will complete the requirements for the degree by Fall of 2027, in Accounting or a closely related field. Other Required Qualifications Expertise in accounting through relevant education, professional experience, teaching, or scholarly work. Capacity to teach accounting courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels in one or more areas, including managerial accounting, auditing, information systems, analytics, or AI. Strong written and verbal communication skills, reflected in the ability to explain complex accounting concepts clearly through written work, presentations, or other professional activities. Ability to contribute to departmental, college, and university service through committee work, academic initiatives, or related activities. Preferred Qualifications Established record of scholarly research and publication, or clear potential to develop one. Evidence of effective teaching at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Research, teaching, and service interests that complement the Accounting Department’s academic programs and initiatives. Ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, students, and other academic or professional partners. Relevant professional accounting experience or credentials, such as CPA certification. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 10/09/2026 Anticipated Close Date 11/5/2026; if posting is still active we are accepting and reviewing applications Special Instructions to Applicants Please include the following as part of your application materials: 1. Cover Letter 2. Resume/CV 3. Contact information for at least three professional references. Position Details Position Number 00112374 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 201001 - Accounting - Poole College of Management EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU website Craigslist Indeed.com Carolina Job Finder/Employment Guide NC Works Dress for Success Technical/Trade School Program Job Fair (Identify Job Fair in question #2 below) Direct Contact from NSCU Representative (identify person in question #2 below) Other Monster.com Other online job board NCSU employee referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Ohter) If you learned about this vacancy from \"other\" or were asked for additional information in question #1, please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
