    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236089": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Scholar",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191787PD Position Number 00112384 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 111801 - Entomology and Plant Pathology Department 111801 - Entomology and Plant Pathology Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties Organization/Department Overview The Department of Entomology and Plant Pathology ( EPP ) in the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences ( CALS ) at North Carolina State University is a Land-Grant University department with more than 40 faculty engaged in teaching, research, and extension programs addressing issues in entomology, plant pathology, and related biological sciences. The Department provides a rich environment for undergraduate and graduate education, research training, and interdisciplinary collaboration, with opportunities to apply current technologies and approaches in laboratory, greenhouse, and field settings. EPP houses several specialized facilities and resources that support research, education, and extension, including the Plant Disease and Insect Clinic, Larry Grand Mycological Herbarium, Micropropagation and Repository Unit, Structural Pest Management Training Facility, Insect Museum, and Center for Integrated Fungal Research. The Department’s programs are supported by the broader resources of CALS , which includes 12 academic departments, extensive research facilities, and research stations located throughout North Carolina that facilitate collaboration with agricultural producers, stakeholders, and industry partners. Primary Purpose of Position The Postdoctoral Scholar will contribute to the interdisciplinary research project “Characterization of the Maize Pattern-Triggered Immunity Response.” The position will investigate the genetic, molecular, and microbiological mechanisms underlying pattern-triggered immunity in maize through research conducted in laboratory, greenhouse, and field settings. The scholar will work collaboratively with Dr. Anna Whitfield and Dr. Peter Balint-Kurti at North Carolina State University, as well as collaborators at the University of Illinois under the supervision of Dr. Tiffany Jamann. Specific research objectives and experimental approaches will be developed in consultation with the principal investigators and will evolve based on project needs and research findings. The scholar will be expected to exercise scientific independence in planning and conducting experiments, interpreting results, communicating findings, and contributing to scholarly publications. Duties and Responsibilities: Planning and Conducting Research – 60% Plan and conduct research in genetics, molecular biology, microbiology, and plant-microbe interactions in laboratory, greenhouse, and field environments. Develop and execute controlled experiments designed to address project objectives and research questions. Apply appropriate experimental designs, controls, protocols, and methodologies to ensure the quality and reproducibility of research findings. Maintain accurate, comprehensive, and organized records of experimental procedures, observations, and results. Analyze and troubleshoot experimental approaches and modify research methods as appropriate based on results and project needs. Collaborate with principal investigators, project team members, and external collaborators to coordinate research activities and advance project objectives. Interpreting, Presenting, and Publishing Research Results – 40% Analyze and interpret experimental results using appropriate scientific approaches and in consultation with project investigators and collaborators. Communicate research findings to principal investigators, collaborators, laboratory and departmental audiences, and other scientific stakeholders. Present research findings at professional meetings, conferences, seminars, and other scientific venues. Prepare research reports, abstracts, presentations, and manuscripts for publication in peer-reviewed scientific journals. Lead and contribute to the development, revision, and submission of manuscripts and other scholarly products resulting from the research. Incorporate feedback from collaborators and peer review Other Work/Responsibilities The Postdoctoral Scholar will participate in research meetings, project discussions, seminars, and other professional development activities within the Department and with collaborating institutions. The scholar will contribute to a collaborative and interdisciplinary research environment, maintain appropriate research and laboratory records, and comply with university, laboratory, and research-related policies and procedures. The position may also involve mentoring or providing guidance to graduate and undergraduate students participating in related research activities, as appropriate. The scholar will be expected to maintain professional expertise through engagement with current scientific literature, professional organizations, conferences, and other scholarly activities relevant to the project. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday - Friday / 8am - 5pm Department Required Skills Ph.D in Genetics, Plant Biology, Plant Pathology or related discipline Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Skills in Molecular biology (manipulation of DNA , RNA and proteins), Plant Pathology, Microbiology and detailed understanding of mendelian and quantitative genetics Skills in statistical data analysis Required License or Certification NC Driver’s License Valid NC Driver's License required? Yes Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $58,656-$62,000 If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 10/12/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236088 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236085": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Scholar",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach a Cover Letter, resume/CV, and contact information for three (3) professional references. Please make sure that the information entered on the application matches what is on your resume. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191786PD Position Number 00112385 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 118101 - Biological And Agricultural Engineering Department 118101 - Biological And Agricultural Engineering Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties The Department of Biological and Agricultural Engineering at North Carolina State University invites applications for a full-time Postdoctoral Research Associate to work with Dr. Daniela Jones, Associate Professor, in machine learning, AI surrogate modeling, and scientific model validation for large-scale agricultural and bioeconomy systems. The position supports REFRAME (Resource Engineering Framework for Responsible, Augmented Modeling and Engagement), a multi-year initiative funded by Schmidt Sciences through the Virtual Institute for Feedstocks of the Future ( VIFF ). REFRAME is developing a modular, AI-enabled, open-source platform that integrates legacy scientific models, artificial intelligence, optimization, and shared data infrastructure to evaluate future biomass systems across availability, accessibility, characterization, conversion, and impacts. The successful candidate will serve as REFRAME’s scientific lead for AI surrogate methodology, providing project-wide leadership in the development, statistical validation, benchmarking, deployment, and long-term evolution of scalable AI surrogate models. Housed within REFRAME’s Modeling Pillar, the researcher will work at the intersection of AI and agricultural domain science and collaborate with an interdisciplinary team of graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, faculty, software developers, the Platform Architect, and researchers within the Digital Backbone and Stakeholder Engagement Pillars. The position will also contribute to AI agents for model orchestration, scientific workflow automation, and stakeholder-facing decision support. The position is expected to begin in Spring 2027, with an initial one-year appointment and the potential for extension based on performance and funding availability. The Postdoctoral Research Associate will: Lead the development and implementation of project-wide methodologies for the development, evaluation, statistical validation, benchmarking, and deployment of scalable and scientifically rigorous AI surrogate models across REFRAME’s modeling domains. Develop generalized surrogate modeling and statistical evaluation frameworks for computationally intensive scientific models, including approaches for calibration, uncertainty quantification, generalization and robustness assessment, and explainable AI. Apply knowledge of agricultural production systems, agronomic practices, crop and soil processes, and biomass systems to evaluate the scientific and practical plausibility of surrogate model behavior and outputs. Collaborate with and mentor interdisciplinary researchers developing AI surrogates while establishing standardized, reproducible scientific machine learning workflows across REFRAME . Collaborate with the Digital Backbone team to integrate validated surrogates into scalable, open-source infrastructure and contribute to AI agents for model orchestration, workflow automation, and scientific decision support. Lead and contribute to peer-reviewed publications and conference presentations, and contribute to research proposal development and the pursuit of external funding opportunities that advance REFRAME and related research Other Work/Responsibilities Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday – Friday, 8 am-5 pm Department Required Skills Demonstrated research experience in statistical learning, machine learning, scientific computing, predictive modeling, or surrogate modeling. Strong Python programming skills and experience implementing machine learning or statistical modeling workflows. Demonstrated knowledge of or research experience with agricultural, biological, environmental, or related systems. Strong written and verbal communication skills and ability to work effectively within interdisciplinary research teams. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Experience developing AI surrogate models, emulators, or scientific machine learning methods. Experience with rigorous model validation, uncertainty quantification, calibration, sensitivity analysis, explainable AI, or assessment of model generalization. Experience with advanced statistical or machine learning approaches, such as deep learning, ensemble methods, Gaussian processes, Bayesian methods, or probabilistic machine learning. Experience working with large scientific or simulation datasets and developing reproducible scientific or open-source software. Experience using high-performance computing ( HPC ), including GPU -enabled, on-premises cluster, or shared server environments, for large-scale scientific computing or machine learning workflows. Experience applying computational methods to agricultural, agronomic, biological, environmental, or bioeconomy systems. Experience mentoring graduate or undergraduate researchers. Required License or Certification Valid NC driver’s license Valid NC Driver's License required? Yes Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $62,000-$72,000 If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 10/09/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/235971 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Briefly, please describe your research experience with agricultural, biological, environmental, or related systems. (Open Ended Question) * Briefly, please describe your experience mentoring graduate/undergraduate students. (Open Ended Question) * Do you, or will you, have a Ph.D. in Statistics, Data Science, Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Agricultural Engineering, Biological Engineering, Industrial Engineering, Operations Research, Applied Mathematics, Computational Science, or a closely related quantitative discipline? Yes No * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently located in Raleigh, or are you willing and able to relocate to Raleigh within the start timeframe? Yes No * Do you have a valid NC driver's license or the ability to obtain one prior to your start date? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Contact Information for References Resume/CV Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236079": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Assistant/Associate/Professor - Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Open Rank - Assistant/Associate/Professor - Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Open Rank - Assistant/Associate/Professor - Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include the following materials with your online application: 1. Cover Letter 2. Resume/CV 3. Research plan (3-5 pages) 4. Teaching plan (2-3 pages) 5. Outreach and engagement plan (1 page) (Other document 1) 6. Names and contact information of three references 7. Up to three representative publications (Other document 2, 3, 4) To ensure full consideration, all application materials should be received by Nov. 15, 2026 . Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194951EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Open Rank - Assistant/Associate/Professor - Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with education and experience: Assistant: $115,000 – $120,000 Associate: $125,000 – $160,000 Full: $160,000 – $250,000 Work Schedule Core Business Hours: Monday - Friday; 8:00 am - 5:00 pm; hours will vary based on teaching and research needs. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Chemical & Biomolecular Engineering About the Department The primary function of the Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering Department is to provide educational programs leading to BS, MS and PhD degrees in Chemical Engineering. The vision of the department is to be a global leader in chemical and biomolecular engineering education and research. The Department offers exciting opportunities for professional growth, a creative and collaborative atmosphere of multidisciplinary research and innovative teaching, and strong ties to the Golden LEAF Biomanufacturing Training and Education Center ( BTEC ). It is integrated within the vibrant and future-oriented science community in the Research Triangle area. NC State is located in Raleigh, one of the fastest-growing and best places to live in the country. The department is ranked #17 in USNWR undergraduate rankings of Chemical Engineering programs, #21 in the USNWR graduate rankings, and #4 in federal research expenditures among ChE departments in the US according to the NSF . To find out more, see http://www.cbe.ncsu.edu . Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering at NC State University seeks highly qualified candidates to fill tenure-track or tenured faculty positions. We particularly encourage applications in the areas of energy or soft materials, with particular emphasis on integration of autonomous laboratories, AI, or machine learning in these fields. Your expertise and contributions will complement departmental strengths in energy and sustainability, materials, and data and computational engineering. Key responsibilities: Develop an externally funded research program of international reputation, including collaborative and interdisciplinary research. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in chemical engineering, including topics in AI and machine learning. Perform departmental service, including committee work, as well as engage in broader initiatives that support the education and research missions of the institution. Contribute to the broader engineering community through professional service. If you are driven by original thinking and collaboration, we invite you to join the Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering at NC State University. Other Responsibilities n/a Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience All Ranks must have the following: Doctoral degree in chemical engineering or a closely related discipline. Ability and willingness to participate in Department, college, and university affairs. Additional Minimum Qualifications by Rank: Assistant Professor: Demonstrated ability and potential to direct activities in mutually agreed-upon areas of responsibility. Associate Professor: Demonstrated ability to direct activities in mutually agreed-upon areas of responsibility. Recognized ability and potential for distinction. Professor: Distinguished achievement and demonstrated ability to direct activities in mutually agreed-upon areas of responsibility. Established reputation in the individual’s profession. Other Required Qualifications Demonstrated expertise in a relevant area of chemical engineering aligned with the department’s teaching or research needs. Proven ability to communicate technical concepts effectively in teaching, research, or other professional settings. Evidence of scholarly contributions, such as peer-reviewed publications, appropriate to the position’s rank and career stage. Preferred Qualifications n/a Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 10/12/2026 Anticipated Close Date Open until filled with applications received by 11/15/2026 guaranteed for full consideration. Special Instructions to Applicants Please include the following materials with your online application: 1. Cover Letter 2. Resume/CV 3. Research plan (3-5 pages) 4. Teaching plan (2-3 pages) 5. Outreach and engagement plan (1 page) (Other document 1) 6. Names and contact information of three references 7. Up to three representative publications (Other document 2, 3, 4) To ensure full consideration, all application materials should be received by Nov. 15, 2026 . Position Details Position Number 00000622 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 140201 - Chemical & Biomolecular Engineering EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have your PHD in a field appropriate for this faculty position? No Response Yes, I have my PHD at this time No, I do not have my PHD at this time, however, I will have it completed the anticipated start date No, I do not have my PHD at this time, nor will I have it completed the anticipated start date Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Other Document (1) Other Document (2) Contact Information for References Research Statement Teaching Statement Resume/CV Optional Documents Other Document (3) Other Document (4) NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
