    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/235822": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Population Medicine and Career Success",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant/Associate Professor of Population Medicine and Career Success Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant/Associate Professor of Population Medicine and Career Success Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include a cover letter, CV, and contact information for at least three professional references. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194878EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Population Medicine and Career Success Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with Education and Experience Work Schedule Monday - Friday, General Business Hours Job Location Raleigh, NC Department College Of Veterinary Medicine About the Department The NC State University College of Veterinary Medicine ( CVM ) is nationally and internationally recognized for leadership in comparative medicine and translational biomedical research. The College leverages access to a state-of-the-art veterinary teaching hospital serving over 32,000 patients annually and maintains strategic collaborations with Duke University, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, and partners across the Research Triangle Park biotechnology ecosystem. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Assistant/Associate Professor of Population Medicine and Career Success specializes in Large Animal Population Medicine and Veterinary Education Scholarship. This dynamic role is designed for an innovative educator and researcher ready to shape the future of veterinary medicine by blending cutting-edge clinical instruction with ground-breaking educational research. This position plays a central role in delivering our core DVM curriculum while building a nationally recognized research program that drives innovation in farm animal health, AI integration, immersive learning, and student well-being. Teaching: Based on specific focus, this faculty member will contribute to population medicine and career readiness teaching in existing core, elective and selective courses. The faculty member will also have the option to participate in teaching and/or proposing new selective, elective or special topics courses. Interested individuals may contribute to ongoing development of house officer and graduate student competency-based training programs and trainee assessments. Research : This position is expected to establish an impactful, nationally recognized research program at the intersection of Large Animal Population Medicine and Veterinary Education Scholarship. This dual-focus program will address critical gaps in population health education by actively developing, implementing, and evaluating novel teaching methods. This position will focus on discovery that interrogates, innovates and transforms farm animal population health and career readiness training in veterinary education. The research will address gaps in knowledge and pivotal questions including, but not limited to, the following examples: Immersive Technologies and Virtual Reality (VR): Investigating the design, implementation, and educational efficacy of immersive virtual environments—such as “digital twin” models of production facilities, processing plants, or pasture ecosystems. This research will leverage VR to simulate complex, high-stakes population medicine scenarios (e.g., biosecurity breaches, foreign animal disease outbreaks, and large-scale herd epidemiology mapping). The focus will be on assessing how immersive environments support rapid systemic decision-making, epidemiological risk assessment, and spatial problem-solving without inducing real-world biosecurity or animal welfare risks. Competency-Based Veterinary Education ( CBVE ) & Advanced Assessments: Developing and validating robust, outcomes-based assessment methodologies. This includes creating standard-setting tools that reliably evaluate both technical execution (e.g., simulation-based herd analytics or theriogenology models) and non-technical professional competencies (e.g., communication, animal welfare advocacy, and One Health system collaboration). Experiential, Simulation, and Community-Engaged Learning: Evaluating the educational efficacy and scalable impact of ambulatory training and community-partnered outreach to bridge the gap between tertiary referral environments and general production practice. Comparing student learning outcomes relevant to population medicine in different clinical settings. Professional Identity Formation ( PIF ) and Career Sustainability: Investigating the longitudinal development of professional identity in DVM students and its explicit correlation to post-graduation career satisfaction, practitioner retention, and mental well-being. This research will evaluate how educational interventions, mentorship, and hidden curricula influence the psychological transition from student to clinician. Specifically, it will look at how to cultivate a resilient, “challenge-focused” professional identity within large animal and population medicine—equipping graduates to find career satisfaction while navigating the unique systemic, environmental, and socio-economic pressures intrinsic to production animal practice. Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Digital Literacy: Investigating the integration of generative AI, intelligent tutoring systems, and clinical decision support models into the DVM curriculum. Research will evaluate how to foster AI literacy and “appropriate skepticism” while examining the cognitive risks of overreliance, algorithmic bias, and data privacy in production animal surveillance. This individual will join existing large and farm animal faculty and staff currently teaching population medicine and epidemiology in DVM years 1-4. Other Responsibilities Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience DVM (or equivalent degree) Other Required Qualifications Excellent communication skills. Experience with extramurally funded research programs. A record of collegial and productive interactions with faculty, staff and students. Interest and enthusiasm for training and mentorship, particularly with regard to graduate students, house officers, and/or postdoctoral fellows. Comfort and experience working with highly interdisciplinary and collaborative faculty. Preferred Qualifications Evidence of relevant advanced training, i.e. DACVIM , DACVPM , EdD, PhD, Masters, (or equivalent degree), and/or teaching certification. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/15/2026 Anticipated Close Date Open until filled Special Instructions to Applicants Please include a cover letter, CV, and contact information for at least three professional references. Position Details Position Number 00112310 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 190101 - College Of Veterinary Medicine EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you currently hold a DVM or equivalent; MD or equivalent; PhD or equivalent? Yes No Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/235821": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Large Animal Clinical Skills and Career Success",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant/Associate Professor of Large Animal Clinical Skills and Career Success Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant/Associate Professor of Large Animal Clinical Skills and Career Success Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include a resume, CV, and contact information for at least three professional references. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194872EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Large Animal Clinical Skills and Career Success Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with Education and Experience Work Schedule Monday - Friday, General Business Hours Job Location Raleigh, NC Department College Of Veterinary Medicine About the Department The NC State University College of Veterinary Medicine ( CVM ) is nationally and internationally recognized for leadership in comparative medicine and translational biomedical research. The College leverages access to a state-of-the-art veterinary teaching hospital serving over 32,000 patients annually and maintains strategic collaborations with Duke University, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, and partners across the Research Triangle Park biotechnology ecosystem. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Assistant/Associate Professor of Large Animal Clinical Skills and Career Success will join a dedicated group of faculty and staff currently teaching large animal clinical skills, medicine and surgery. A combination of models, simulations and farm animals at the Teaching Animal Unit and Reedy Creek Farm are used to facilitate assessments that can be used to develop skills portfolios and investigate best practices in feedback and remediation of clinical skills. Teaching: This faculty member will contribute to clinical skills, large animal and career readiness teaching in existing core, elective and selective courses. The faculty member will also have the option to participate in teaching and/or proposing new selective or elective courses. Interested individuals may contribute to ongoing development of house officer and graduate student competency-based training programs and trainee assessments. Research : This faculty member will establish an impactful and nationally recognized research program dedicated to advancing Large Animal Clinical Skills educational research. As veterinary curricula globally evolve to meet changing technological, societal, and agricultural needs, this position will drive evidence-based advancements in how veterinary students acquire, refine, and maintain large animal technical and clinical competencies. The faculty member will be expected to investigate current high-priority areas and address critical, unmapped gaps in knowledge within veterinary medical education. The prospective areas of educational research supported by this position include, but are not limited to: Simulation-Based Learning & Physical Model Innovation: Developing, validating, and optimizing large animal (equine, bovine, and production animal) procedural models, simulators and assessments (i.e. OSCEs, mini- CEX , etc.). A primary research gap in this domain is the critical lack of longitudinal data assessing the long-term transferability of skills from synthetic simulators to live animal clinical scenarios to practice, as well as addressing the historical “small animal bias” in existing commercial simulation tools. Artificial Intelligence (AI) & Digital Workflow Integration: Exploring the integration of generative AI, multimodal large language models, and AI-standardized stakeholders within clinical training and communication workflows. Research will target how to teach students to utilize AI safely, ethically, and responsibly for diagnostic reasoning and uncertainty management, while addressing student adoption challenges, cognitive overreliance, and technological biases. Competency-Based Veterinary Education ( CBVE ) & Assessment: Designing, implementing, and validating objective, standardized assessment instruments and grading frameworks for psychomotor skills. Research will focus on mapping competencies to pedagogical combinations that offer the highest cost-benefit ratios and efficacy for equine and production animal training. Remediation Strategies & Cognitive Load Management: Developing evidence-based intervention and remediation strategies for students experiencing difficulties with technical proficiency. This includes studying methods to lower student anxiety and ensure safety during the high-stakes transition from low-stress models to live, potentially unpredictable large animals. Spectrum of Care, Ethics, & Community-Engaged Learning: Investigating educational frameworks that prepare students to practice quality medicine across a spectrum of care, particularly in resource-limited, rural, or underserved environments. Research could address how experiential learning in these settings impacts clinical skill acquisition and influences veterinary workforce shortages in production animal medicine. Community-based Education Models & Educator Development: Assessing how the pedagogical characteristics, instructional proficiency, professional identity and career satisfaction of clinical educators affect student learning in off-campus clinical teaching environments. Research will target frameworks for standardizing educator professional development and mentoring ability among non-faculty clinical preceptors. Pipeline Development, Admissions Predictors, & Career Sustainability: Investigating the correlation between holistic DVM admissions criteria (e.g., non-cognitive attributes, rural or agricultural backgrounds, specific pre-veterinary experiences) and long-term career commitment to large animal and food supply veterinary medicine. Research in this domain will target the critical “pipeline leak”—the documented decline in large animal career interest that occurs over the course of the four-year professional curriculum. Prospective studies will explore how educational interventions, early tracking pathways, mentorship frameworks, and systemic support systems can mitigate burnout, bridge the pay-to-debt gap, and ensure the geographic and economic sustainability of the large animal veterinary workforce in rural and underserved areas. Wellbeing, Professional Identity, & Veterinary Humanities: Evaluating the intersections of clinical skills mastery with veterinary humanities, ethical reasoning, and professional identity formation. The program will examine how early, structured competence in large animal handling correlates with student self-care, resilience, and long-term career sustainability. Other Responsibilities Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience DVM (or equivalent degree) Other Required Qualifications Excellent communication skills. Experience with extramurally funded research programs. A record of collegial and productive interactions with faculty, staff and students. Interest and enthusiasm for training and mentorship, particularly with regard to graduate students, house officers, and/or postdoctoral fellows. Comfort and experience working with highly interdisciplinary and collaborative faculty. Preferred Qualifications Evidence of relevant advanced training, i.e. DACVIM , DACVS , EdD, PhD, M.Ed, Ed.M., (or equivalent degree), and/or teaching certification. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/11/2026 Anticipated Close Date Open until filled Special Instructions to Applicants Please include a resume, CV, and contact information for at least three professional references. Position Details Position Number 00112309 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 190101 - College Of Veterinary Medicine EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you currently hold a DVM or equivalent; MD or equivalent; PhD or equivalent? Yes No Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/235819": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Scholar",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include the Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191354PD Position Number 00111102 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 140401 - Electrical & Computer Engineering Department 140401 - Electrical & Computer Engr. Job City & State Raleigh, NC-27606 Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties The Department of Electrical Engineering (College of Engineering) and the College of Sciences (Department of Physics, Department of Mathematics) are searching for two (2) Postdoctoral Research Scholars in quantum computing at NC State University. The two positions will work synergistically on hybrid continuous-discrete-variable quantum computing, broadly defined. One position will focus on condensed matter physics, quantum simulation; the other position will focus on compilation, benchmark, and HPC simulation of quantum circuits. The postdocs will work with a cluster of vibrant quantum computing faculty at NC State, including Dr. Bojko Bakalov, Professor (Mathematics), Dr. Dror Baron (Electrical and Computer Engineering), Lex Kemper (Physics), Yuan Liu (Electrical and Computer Engineering, Computer Science, and Physics), Frank Mueller (Computer Science), and Huiyang Zhou (Electrical and Computer Engineering), with possible external collaborations with other universities and national lab. Other Duties and Responsibilities Explore relevant parameter regions for useful boson-fermi mixed quantum matter; Design, develop, and implement novel quantum algorithms to simulate them. Quantify resource requirements on simulation on hybrid CD-DV quantum processors under noise, and compare to qubit-based quantum computers; Explore compilation, benchmarking, HPC simulation, error mitigation, and error correction strategies on hybrid CV-DV quantum processors; Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams to understand domain-specific requirements and integrate discoveries into the team’s mission; Help to lead the project and mentor junior researchers; Publish research findings in reputable journals and conferences Other Work/Responsibilities Supervising and mentoring graduate students Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here , and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday-Friday Department Required Skills N/A Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Experience with one of the following fields is preferred but not required: quantum computing, quantum algorithms, quantum simulation, quantum optics, quantum compilation, classical simulation and benchmarking of quantum circuits, condensed matter physics, programming, error correction, and signal processing Required License or Certification N/A Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $60,176 - $70,000 If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many 2 Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 09/10/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/209539 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/235773": {
      "title": "Open Rank Teaching Faculty",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Open Rank Teaching Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Open Rank Teaching Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include as a part of your application: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter Teaching Statement (1-2 pages) Teaching Portfolio (other document 1): a table listing a few relevant courses and/or most frequently taught courses(max 10 courses) taught as instructor of record; Include course title, level (undergraduate/graduate), delivery mode (online/in person/hybrid), number of times taught, and approximate number of students; If you have not been instructor of record, list all courses you have served as a TA and your responsibilities in that course. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194875EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Open Rank Teaching Faculty Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with education and experience: (Asst Teaching Professor: $120,000 – $130,000; Assoc Teaching Professor: $130,000 – $145,000; Teaching Professor: $145,000 – $160,000) Work Schedule Monday through Friday, 8 am to 5 pm (additional work outside of standard hours may be required due to business needs) Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Institute for Advanced Analytics About the Department Established in 2007, the NC State University Institute for Advanced Analytics ( IAA ) is a global leader in graduate analytics education. The Institute prepares future analytics professionals through an immersive, interdisciplinary curriculum integrating statistics, data science, artificial intelligence, machine learning, operations research, and business strategy. The Institute’s flagship Master of Science in Analytics ( MSA ) program is complemented by a growing portfolio of professional education and online certificate programs designed to meet the evolving workforce needs of industry. The Institute maintains strong partnerships with corporate, government, and nonprofit organizations to provide applied learning experiences that prepare graduates and working professionals to solve complex, data-driven business challenges. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Institute for Advanced Analytics invites applications for an open-rank Assistant, Associate, or full Teaching Professor. This 12-month non-tenure-track faculty position will play a central role in developing, delivering, and continuously improving the Institute’s portfolio of online professional certificate programs and graduate instruction. As a faculty member, you will shape how working professionals and graduate students learn and apply analytics in a rapidly evolving field. You will bring your expertise in analytics, artificial intelligence, machine learning, and data science into the classroom while creating practical, technology-enabled learning experiences that connect academic knowledge to real-world challenges. Through teaching, mentoring, curriculum innovation, and collaboration with faculty and industry partners, you will help prepare learners to apply emerging tools and insights in their professional work. Key Responsibilities fall within the following functional areas: Online Curriculum Development and Teaching: Lead the design, development, delivery, and continuous improvement of online certificate and graduate courses, creating engaging content and assessments that support meaningful learning outcomes. Create engaging asynchronous and synchronous learning experiences using modern educational technologies and evidence-based instructional practices. Continuously strengthen curriculum by incorporating advances in analytics and emerging technologies and using student feedback and assessment data to improve learning experiences. Partner with faculty, instructional designers, educational technology professionals, and media specialists to deliver high-quality online learning experiences. Deliver graduate and professional education courses in analytics and related disciplines. Student Engagement and Applied Learning: Mentor graduate students through industry-sponsored projects, connecting them with corporate partners and guiding teams from planning through final deliverables. Provide academic and professional advising through regular student engagement and office hours. Supervise graduate teaching assistants as assigned. Foster a collaborative learning environment that supports student growth and professional development. Program Development and Professional Engagement: Help shape professional education offerings in response to emerging workforce needs and opportunities. Partner with faculty, Institute leadership, and industry stakeholders to strengthen curriculum and experiential learning. Contribute to program assessment, accreditation, recruitment, outreach, and executive education activities. Build relationships with industry partners that expand learning and professional opportunities for students. Service and Scholarly Engagement: Contribute to Institute and university committees, admissions, curriculum planning, and faculty governance. Maintain current expertise through professional development in analytics education, instructional technology, and industry trends. Pursue scholarly and professional activities aligned with your expertise and rank, including applied research, presentations, publications, consulting, or industry collaboration. If you are energized by helping learners translate analytics and emerging technologies into meaningful solutions, we invite you to bring your expertise to a faculty community committed to innovation, applied learning, and the evolving needs of today’s workforce. Other Responsibilities n/a Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Assistant Teaching Professor Doctoral degree, equivalent degree, or equivalent professional experience in analytics, data science, statistics, computer science, information systems, operations research, business analytics, artificial intelligence, or a closely related discipline. Expertise in one or more areas of analytics or data science. Teaching, training, or curriculum development experience with graduate-level courses. Ability to communicate complex analytics concepts effectively with students, faculty, and industry partners. Associate Teaching Professor: In addition to the qualifications for Assistant Teaching Professor: Established record of teaching experience in higher education, executive education, or professional training. Record of developing curriculum or educational programs. Leadership in professional practice, industry, or applied analytics. Demonstrated contributions to academic service or program leadership. Teaching Professor: In addition to the qualifications for Associate Teaching Professor: National or international recognition as a leader in analytics or a related field. Distinguished record of curriculum innovation, educational programs, or industry initiatives. Sustained impact through teaching, professional engagement, and service. Proven leadership that advances analytics in higher education, industry, or both. Other Required Qualifications n/a Preferred Qualifications Background in designing and teaching fully online or hybrid courses. Experience with learning management systems such as Moodle or Canvas. Industry expertise applying analytics, artificial intelligence, machine learning, or data science to business challenges. Knowledge of online instructional design and quality frameworks, such as Quality Matters. Record of developing partnerships with industry or external organizations. Required License(s) or Certification(s) n/a Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/17/2026 Anticipated Close Date 10/26/2026; If posting is still active we are accepting and reviewing applications Special Instructions to Applicants Please include as a part of your application: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter Teaching Statement (1-2 pages) Teaching Portfolio (other document 1): a table listing a few relevant courses and/or most frequently taught courses(max 10 courses) taught as instructor of record; Include course title, level (undergraduate/graduate), delivery mode (online/in person/hybrid), number of times taught, and approximate number of students; If you have not been instructor of record, list all courses you have served as a TA and your responsibilities in that course. Position Details Position Number 00112317 Position Type Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 020301 - Advanced Analytics EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Other Document (1) Teaching Statement Optional Documents Contact Information for References NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
