    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/235392": {
      "title": "Systems Librarian",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Systems Librarian Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Systems Librarian Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the required application fully and accurately. Attach a cover letter, resume, and contact information for four (4) current professional references. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194911EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Systems Librarian Anticipated Hiring Range $80,000 minimum Work Schedule University Business hours are Monday - Friday 8AM - 5PM. The Libraries supports flexible work arrangements based on departmental and operational needs. This position will require some onsite work. Exempt position. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Libraries About the Department Join the NC State University Libraries and help us create adventurous, innovative services and library spaces that delight students, faculty, and researchers. The award-winning James B. Hunt Jr. Library on NC State’s Centennial Campus , offers access to advanced technologies that are enabling revolutionary ways to see and use information. Capturing NC State’s spirit of innovation in education and research, the Hunt Library is recognized as one of the world’s most creative and inspirational learning and collaborative spaces and a model for “the library of the future.” The D. H. Hill Jr. Library , serving the main campus , combines the best of tradition and innovation, housing special collections and a beautiful gallery alongside vibrant, experiential spaces for making, digital media creation, data analysis and visualization, and collaboration. Three branch libraries focus on design, natural resources, and veterinary medicine. The NC State University Libraries invites applications and nominations for the position of Systems Librarian in the Digital Library Initiatives department. The Digital Library Initiatives ( DLI ) department applies systems analysis, design, service development, and software development skills to the creation and improvement of a broad range of library products and services. As a collaborative and consultative partner, DLI works with stakeholders across the Libraries and university to bring new services to life and solve complex technical challenges. DLI develops and supports the core systems that provide access to the Libraries’ print and electronic resources, including Ex Libris Alma, the Primo discovery layer, ILLiad, and EZproxy. The department maintains a broad portfolio of prototype and production systems and services in areas including digital collections, high-technology spaces, researcher profiles and identifiers, exploratory applications of machine learning and AI, and assessment and analytics. DLI develops new research infrastructure support services focused on improving the efficiency and productivity of NC State researchers in collaboration with university partners including the Office of Information Technology ( OIT ) and the Office of Research and Innovation ( ORI ). Staff develop and support open source and locally developed applications that promote resource discovery and delivery, enable use of Libraries spaces, and improve staff workflows. For examples of the department’s projects and initiatives, visit: https://www.lib.ncsu.edu/dli/projects Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Systems Librarian provides primary administration and project management for the Libraries’ Ex Libris Alma platform and public-facing Primo discovery layer. The position facilitates collaborative decision-making for these discovery tools, including chairing the Libraries’ Alma Product Team and working with all library services platform teams to align system policies with user and departmental needs. The position translates complex technical developments into clear, functional workflows for colleagues, helping to optimize processes across functional areas, including fulfillment, acquisitions, resource management, resource sharing, and user experience. They partner with other stakeholders to manage the Alma platform’s lifecycle, including monitoring software release schedules, assessing their impacts on library operations, utilizing analytics to generate reports for data-informed decision-making, implementing configuration updates, maintaining technical documentation, and providing functional support for library staff. The position acts as a primary technical liaison with Ex Libris and participates actively in professional communities such as ELUNA , the UNC System, and the Triangle Research Libraries Network ( TRLN ). They actively explore emerging services and technologies, including AI-driven improvements to library search, discovery, and internal workflows, working to enhance the library user experience. The position deeply considers how their approach to their daily work reflects and advances the Libraries’ Strategic Plan , creating an environment and community that is welcoming for both patrons and colleagues alike. The position works closely with colleagues throughout the Libraries and with university partners, participates in library planning, and serves on library and campus-wide committees, task forces, and teams. Librarians are expected to be active professionally and to contribute to developments in the field. The position reports to the Discovery Systems Manager in Digital Library Initiatives. This position is based in North Carolina. This position is eligible for flexible hours with a hybrid work environment and will require occasional onsite work. NC State promotes an integrated approach to problem solving that transforms lives and provides leadership for social, economic, and technological development across North Carolina and around the world. NC State’s land grant mission of teaching, research and service is dedicated to the service of North Carolina and its people. Applicants are encouraged to review the institution’s mission, vision and strategic plan, and consider how their background, interest and experience would enable them to support the university. Other Responsibilities Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience ALA -accredited MLS , MIS , or equivalent advanced degree, such as in Computer Science or Information Technology Other Required Qualifications Applicants are encouraged to think broadly about and communicate how their skills and experiences transfer to the qualifications below, including in ways that may not be obvious, such as how non-library-specific skills and experiences speak to the position responsibilities. We strongly encourage and welcome applicants with a variety of backgrounds, interests, and experiences to apply for this position. Demonstrated experience providing support or administration for an integrated library system (e.g., Alma, Sierra) Ability to manage multiple projects from planning to completion, including coordinating with cross-departmental collaborators, facilitating meetings, and maintaining project documentation Experience diagnosing and resolving complex technical issues involving library software, data integrity, system performance, and user experience Ability to foster an environment of belonging and well-being Ability to communicate clearly and knowledgeably across audiences with varied technical backgrounds Ability to work independently, creatively, and collaboratively in a team environment, including with colleagues across multiple functional specialties. Evidence of ability for ongoing professional development and contribution Preferred Qualifications It is not required that candidates meet any of the preferred qualifications to be considered for this position. The following skills represent some of the areas in which this position could potentially grow and focus, based on the incumbent’s background and interests. Experience with Ex Libris Alma and Primo and related ExLibris products (e.g., Rapido, Leganto) Experience with languages such as Python, SQL and with the Linux command line to automate routine tasks and create custom integrations via APIs Experience serving as a lead technical liaison with product vendors Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/25/2026 Anticipated Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Please complete the required application fully and accurately. Attach a cover letter, resume, and contact information for four (4) current professional references. Position Details Position Number 00112318 Position Type Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 250101 - Libraries EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/235361": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In addition to your application, please upload the following: Cover Letter CV Research statement Teaching statement Full names and contact information of three professional references In “Other Document (1)”, upload up to three representative publications In “Other Document (2)”, upload a statement on existing or planned outreach, engagement, and/or service (<1 page). Candidates should mention the position area with which they are most closely affiliated in the cover letter and in the supplemental questions of the application. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis and will continue until the positions are filled. Initial review will begin on November 5, 2026. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194904EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with rank and experience Work Schedule Core Business Hours: Monday - Friday; 8:00 am - 5:00 pm; hours will vary based on research and teaching needs. Job Location Raleigh, NC 27695 Department Fitts Department of Industrial & Systems Engineering About the Department Why ISE at NC State? In ISE , you will be part of a department where innovative research happens both within and across disciplines. The Fitts Department of Industrial and Systems Engineering includes more than 25 faculty, 10 core staff, 350 undergraduate students, and 250 graduate students, including approximately 75 Ph.D. students. Our research spans advanced and biomedical manufacturing; health systems; human systems; supply chain and logistics; and systems analytics and optimization, along with interdisciplinary collaborations across the university and beyond. Our faculty are internationally recognized in their fields, with Fellows of IISE , INFORMS , SME , and other professional societies. You will join a collaborative and collegial community where faculty work across traditional disciplinary boundaries and engage with researchers, medical schools, universities, industry, and government partners. The department leads three centers and multiple interdisciplinary graduate programs , creating opportunities to pursue research and educational collaborations well beyond ISE . In addition to degrees in ISE , the department leads the professional Master’s in Engineering Management program and collaborates on the graduate Operations Research program. The department houses two state-funded centers that are public-private partnerships: the Ergonomics Center of North Carolina , the only center of its kind at a U.S. public research institution, and the Center for Additive Manufacturing and Logistics , one of the most advanced manufacturing and 3D printing laboratories in the country. The newly established Bezos Center for Alternative Proteins is also led by an ISE faculty member. These centers provide additional opportunities to collaborate with industry and pursue research with real-world impact. You will have access to world-class laboratory and research facilities supporting computing, manufacturing, human factors, and ergonomics research. These resources are complemented by Fitts-Woolard Hall , our state-of-the-art home on NC State’s Centennial Campus, located near the award-winning Hunt Library and numerous industry and government facilities. Centennial Campus provides a unique environment for university-industry collaboration and interdisciplinary research. At NC State ISE , our students “Think and Do” through active learning and real-world problems across the ISE discipline. You will have the opportunity to mentor and teach a diverse and growing student population and help prepare students to become leaders in academia, industry, and government. NC State is also investing significantly in engineering, with up to 40% growth in engineering faculty, staff, and undergraduate and graduate students expected over the coming years , creating new opportunities for collaboration, education, and research. You will also benefit from being in Raleigh and the Research Triangle , one of the nation’s leading centers for technology, research, and innovation. NC State is located within close proximity to Duke University, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, major research institutes, and a wide range of world-class companies. Raleigh offers an exceptional quality of life, with outstanding restaurants, cultural and recreational opportunities, and easy access to both the mountains and the coast. At NC State ISE , you will join a nationally recognized department that values collaboration, innovation, and impact—and a university and community positioned for significant growth. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Industrial and Systems Engineering ( ISE ) at NC State University invites applications for open-rank, tenure-track faculty positions at all career stages. The department welcomes candidates whose research and teaching interests align with the broad field of Industrial and Systems Engineering, with particular interest in artificial intelligence and/or quantum computing for optimization; logistics and supply chain management; data science and analytics; and emerging areas of national and international importance. Appointments may be considered at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor level based on qualifications and career stage. In this role, you will shape the future of Industrial and Systems Engineering through research, teaching, and collaboration. You will have the opportunity to establish a distinctive research agenda, pursue meaningful partnerships across disciplines, and translate your expertise into advances that address complex engineering challenges. Through your teaching and mentorship, you will help prepare the next generation of engineers, researchers, and leaders while contributing your perspective and expertise to the continued growth and excellence of ISE and NC State. Key Responsibilities include and are not limited to the following: Build and sustain an independent, externally funded research program that advances Industrial and Systems Engineering and contributes to emerging areas of national and international importance. Conduct and disseminate high-impact research through scholarly publications, presentations, and other contributions to the field. Develop interdisciplinary collaborations within NC State and with external academic, industry, government, and research partners to address complex engineering challenges. Teach and develop courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels, creating engaging learning experiences that prepare students for the evolving field of Industrial and Systems Engineering. Mentor and advise graduate students and support their academic, research, and professional development. Contribute to the department, college, and university community through service, leadership, and activities that advance the mission and vision of NC State. If you are an innovative researcher and educator ready to advance Industrial and Systems Engineering, collaborate across disciplines, and prepare the next generation of engineering leaders, we encourage you to apply. Other Responsibilities n/a Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Industrial Engineering or a related area along with appropriate experience by their start date: Rank of Assistant Professor – Demonstrated ability and the potential for directing activities in the mutually agreed upon realms of responsibility; ability and willingness to participate in department, college, and university affairs; a doctoral degree in Industrial Engineering or closely-related discipline. Rank of Associate Professor – Recognized ability and potential for distinction, and demonstrated ability to direct activities, in the mutually agreed upon realms of responsibility; demonstrated ability and willingness to participate in department, college, and university affairs; a doctoral degree in Industrial Engineering or closely-related discipline. Rank of Professor – Distinguished achievement, and demonstrated ability to direct activities, in the mutually agreed upon realms of responsibility; established reputation in the individual’s profession; demonstrated ability and willingness to participate in department, college, and university affairs; a doctoral degree in Industrial Engineering or closely-related discipline. Other Required Qualifications Demonstrated expertise in Artificial Intelligence, Optimization, and/or Quantum Computing. Strong methodological foundation and record (or clear potential) for publishing impactful research. Proven ability (or clear potential) to develop and sustain an externally funded research program. Commitment to excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching, advising, and mentorship. Commitment to engaging in outreach and extension as consistent with the mission of the university. Preferred Qualifications N/A Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/24/2026 Anticipated Close Date 11/5/2027; this is a pooled recruitment, we are accepting, reviewing and hiring for several positions at varying ranks throughout the course of this pooled timeframe. Special Instructions to Applicants In addition to your application, please upload the following: Cover Letter CV Research statement Teaching statement Full names and contact information of three professional references In “Other Document (1)”, upload up to three representative publications In “Other Document (2)”, upload a statement on existing or planned outreach, engagement, and/or service (<1 page). Candidates should mention the position area with which they are most closely affiliated in the cover letter and in the supplemental questions of the application. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis and will continue until the positions are filled. Initial review will begin on November 5, 2026. Position Details Position Number 00000500 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.00 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 140601 - Fitts Department of Industrial & Systems Engineering EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Radio / Television Advertisement Professional Organization Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have your PHD in a field appropriate for this faculty position? No Response Yes, I have my PHD at this time No, I do not have my PHD at this time, however, I will have it completed the anticipated start date No, I do not have my PHD at this time, nor will I have it completed the anticipated start date * Which position area are you most closely affiliated with? optimization, especially artificial intelligence quantum computing for optimization logistics and supply chain management data science and analytics Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Contact Information for References Research Statement Teaching Statement Other Document (1) Other Document (2) Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/235246": {
      "title": "Clinical Pathology Residency",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Clinical Pathology Residency Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Clinical Pathology Residency Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Questions related to the application process can be directed to Caitlin Falls in CVM Human Resources. Reference forms and transcripts can be sent to her via email or regular mail. Caitlin Falls NC State University CVM- Human Resources 1060 William Moore Drive Raleigh, NC 27607 Phone: 919-513-6233 Email: cmfalls@ncsu.edu This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191736PD Position Number 00101830 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 196001 - Department of Population Health and Pathobiology Department 196001 - Department of Population Health and Pathobiology Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties The College of Veterinary Medicine at North Carolina State University invites outstanding candidates to apply for a 3-year residency position in veterinary clinical pathology beginning July 2027. The training program focuses on in-depth learning of clinical pathology and ACVP board preparation under the supervision of 4 ACVP board-certified clinical pathologists. The resident will join a busy clinical pathology service and play a role in student education and hospital interactions. In addition, there are local veterinary diagnostic labs and the graduate programs at the CVM draw on abundant resources available in the Research Triangle region (universities, industry, and government) to provide unique research and career opportunities. Applicants must possess a DVM or equivalent degree(s), have an excellent academic record, strong communication skills, and be committed to a career in veterinary clinical pathology. Clinical or a post- DVM experience is desirable. NC State University is near two other major universities (Duke University and the University of North Carolina – Chapel Hill) and the Research Triangle Park, which includes multiple government agencies, non-profit institutes, biotechnology, and large pharmaceutical companies. To view full vacancy announcement, additional requirements, and to apply online, please visit https://jobs.ncsu.edu/ See https://cvm.ncsu.edu/education/residencies/residencies-clinical-pathology/ for program description and additional information. Applications should include (1) a curriculum vitae, (2) statement of career goals, (3) official college and professional school transcripts, and (4) three references (see link to form). We will begin reviewing applications on Oct. 15, 2026, and continue until a suitable candidate is found. The position is available July 15, 2027. The following link is for the reference form which will be in place of traditional letters. Please provide this link to your references https://forms.gle/Mm7Sgb2vBiwhNWZ79 Questions related to the application process can be directed to Caitlin Falls in CVM Human Resources. Reference forms and transcripts can be sent to her via email or regular mail. Other Work/Responsibilities N/A Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule 8am-5pm, Monday-Friday with variability depending on case load; some evening and weekend on-call. Department Required Skills Must have good diagnostic laboratory, teaching and communication skills. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Clinical experience is highly desirable Required License or Certification Eligible for North Carolina Veterinary Licensure and/or faculty certificate under the supervisor of the NCSU College of Veterinary Medicine, Veterinary Health Complex. Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $54,000 If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 07/17/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/232888 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have (or will you have by date of hire) a DVM or equivalent degree? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 Contact Information for References Transcripts 1 (required of finalists) NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
