    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/235228": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Philosophy",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Philosophy Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant Professor of Philosophy Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following to your online application: an application letter explaining your interest in the job, a curriculum vitae , a brief (1-2 page) research statement, evidence of teaching ability, and a writing sample of no more than 12,500 words. In addition to submitting the required application material online, please arrange to have three letters of reference sent by email attachment to Mia Henry at mahenry2@ncsu.edu. The deadline for applications is November 1, 2026. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194874EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant Professor of Philosophy Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with experience and credentials Work Schedule Varies based on teaching schedule Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Philosophy & Religious Studies About the Department The NC State Department of Philosophy and Religious Studies is committed to offering a high-quality undergraduate Philosophy curriculum, including a major and minor in Philosophy, that gives students an opportunity to confront through historical and contemporary resources a wide range of central philosophical issues, such as the relationship between the mind and brain, the ethical implications of scientific advances, the justification of moral, political, and legal institutions, the relationship between human knowledge and reality, and the nature of the logic that structures human language and thought. Offering a high-quality undergraduate Religious Studies curriculum, including a major and a minor in Religious Studies, that provides students an extended opportunity to examine the multiple interpretations of the category “religion” – including religion as a social construction, as an element of psychological development, as a branch of metaphysics, and as a constellation of ritual practices – and the ways in which religious traditions have played a central role in human culture and history; developing the analytical abilities and expressive powers of our students. Providing and expanding educational and research opportunities at the graduate level; and conducting research, teaching and scholarship that further knowledge and understanding in the disciplines of Philosophy and Religious Studies. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The NC State Department of Philosophy and Religious Studies welcomes applications for an appointment as a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Philosophy with expertise in logic. Candidates must have completed a Ph.D. in Philosophy by May 2027. The responsibilities of the appointee will include teaching courses on logic up to and including the advanced level and contributing to the department’s teaching needs in other areas of philosophy. In addition to having a demonstrated ability to teach advanced logic, the ideal candidate will also have a record of philosophical research interests that extend beyond logic proper. The teaching load is two courses per semester. Other responsibilities include research and service. Other Responsibilities Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Ph.D. in Philosophy or closely related field by May 2027 Other Required Qualifications Evidence of teaching effectiveness Superior Communication skills Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching experience at the college level and demonstrated evidence of teaching excellence. Required License(s) or Certification(s) n/a Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/18/2026 Anticipated Close Date 11/01/2026; if posting is still active we are accepting and reviewing applications. Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following to your online application: an application letter explaining your interest in the job, a curriculum vitae , a brief (1-2 page) research statement, evidence of teaching ability, and a writing sample of no more than 12,500 words. In addition to submitting the required application material online, please arrange to have three letters of reference sent by email attachment to Mia Henry at mahenry2@ncsu.edu. The deadline for applications is November 1, 2026. Position Details Position Number 00000874 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 160501 - Philosophy & Religious Studies EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for References Short Writing Sample Teaching Statement Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/235177": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. As part of your application materials please provide the following: 1. Cover letter with a statement of your research interests 2. Curriculum vitae 3. Contact information of three references. Applicants selected for interviews will be asked to provide evidence of their teaching ability (teaching portfolio) and a writing sample (15,000 words maximum), or you may upload them now. The deadline for applications is November 15, 2026. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194885EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant Professor Anticipated Hiring Range $70,000 - $75,000 Work Schedule Varies According to Need Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Integrative Humanities and Social Sciences About the Department The Department of Integrative Humanities and Social Sciences houses six majors with over 500 students in Africana Studies, Arts Studies, International Studies, Self-Design, Science, Technology, and Society, and Women’s, Gender and Sexuality Studies. IHSS also offers 7 undergraduate minors, 3 undergraduate dual-degree honors programs, and 1 graduate program. IHSS has core faculty and faculty directors who work in partnership with departments from our college and others to deliver the courses in each program. IHSS actively partners with departments and programs on campus and in the Triangle to host events including speakers and conferences in support of the programs several times during the school year. For more information, please visit https://ihss.chass.ncsu.edu . The Department of Philosophy and Religious Studies is committed to offering a high-quality undergraduate Philosophy curriculum, including a major and minor in Philosophy. PRS is also committed to offering a high-quality undergraduate Religious Studies curriculum, including a major and a minor in Religious Studies, that provides students an extended opportunity to examine the multiple interpretations of the category “religion” – including religion as a social construction, as an element of psychological development, as a branch of metaphysics, and as a constellation of ritual practices – and the ways in which religious traditions have played a central role in human culture and history; developing the analytical abilities and expressive powers of our students. PRS provides educational and research opportunities at the graduate level; and conducts research, teaching, and scholarship that advances knowledge and understanding in the disciplines of Philosophy and Religious Studies. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties North Carolina State University welcomes applications for an appointment as a tenure-track Assistant Professor with expertise in Hinduism. The faculty position will be housed in the Department of Integrative Humanities and Social Sciences ( IHSS ), with a joint appointment in the Department of Philosophy and Religious Studies ( PRS ). The appointment in IHSS will be based in one of the following programs: International Studies; Science, Technology and Society; Arts Studies; or Women’s, Gender and Sexuality Studies. A research focus on modern and/or contemporary periods preferred. Training in pre-modern languages and cultures welcome. The standard teaching load will be four courses per academic year, with two each in IHSS and PRS . Other responsibilities include research, publication, and service. Other Responsibilities Other duties as assigned by the Department Head. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Successfully defended a PhD in Religious Studies or a closely related field by May 2027. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Other Required Qualifications Demonstrated a capacity to teach courses on Hinduism/South Asian traditions and methods/theory in the study of religion. Proven skills in teaching and facilitating research with a broad cross-section of students. Offer substantial course content in person and online. Commitment to an active research agenda. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Experience working with interdisciplinary subject matter. Strong organizational and time management skills. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching at the university level. Doctoral degree in Religious Studies. Research interests in environmental issues, gender and sexuality, nationalism, politics, subaltern studies, and ethnicity are welcome Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/18/2026 Anticipated Close Date 11/15/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants As part of your application materials please provide the following: 1. Cover letter with a statement of your research interests 2. Curriculum vitae 3. Contact information of three references. Applicants selected for interviews will be asked to provide evidence of their teaching ability (teaching portfolio) and a writing sample (15,000 words maximum), or you may upload them now. The deadline for applications is November 15, 2026. Position Details Position Number 00112328 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 161001 - Integrative Humanities&Soc Sci EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU website Craigslist Indeed.com Carolina Job Finder/Employment Guide NC Works Dress for Success Technical/Trade School Program Job Fair (Identify Job Fair in question #2 below) Direct Contact from NSCU Representative (identify person in question #2 below) Other Monster.com Other online job board NCSU employee referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Ohter) If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for References Optional Documents Short Writing Sample Teaching Statement NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
