    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/235145": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include with your application the following documents: Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Contact Information for References 2-page Teaching Philosophy 2-page Research Statement Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194888EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant Professor Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with experience and credentials Work Schedule Varies Job Location Raleigh, NC Department School of Social Work About the Department North Carolina State University is a research-focused (R1) institution located in the Research Triangle Area, in Raleigh, North Carolina. As a public land-grant institution, NC State has a duty not only to conduct research but also to provide accessible education and to serve the public through extension. Housed in the College of Humanities and Social Sciences, the School of Social Work offers undergraduate and graduate education to approximately 250 students. The BSW generalist social work curriculum prepares students for entry-level social work practice, leadership, and the delivery and evaluation of health and human services, as well as future graduate study. The MSW curriculum prepares students for advanced generalist practice, including leadership in planning, developing, managing, and evaluating culturally relevant services for individuals, families, groups, organizations, and communities. NC State is committed to excellence in research, scholarship, teaching, and community extension and engagement. The School of Social Work is accredited by the Council on Social Work Education ( CSWE ). CSWE’s Commission on Accreditation is the sole body authorized to accredit BSW and MSW programs in the United States. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The School of Social Work invites applications for two tenure-track Assistant Professor positions. Tenure-track and tenured faculty are expected to develop and sustain a strong record of research and scholarship, excel in teaching and advising, engage in community outreach and partnership, and provide service to school, college, university, and profession. We seek candidates with demonstrated expertise in social work theory, practice, research, policy, and a commitment to preparing the next generation of social work professionals. Primary teaching responsibilities will be in the School’s Bachelor of Social Work ( BSW ) program and/or Masters of Social Work ( MSW ) program. The typical teaching load is two courses per semester. Other Responsibilities Other duties as assigned by the Head of the School of Social Work. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Ph.D. in social work or a closely related field, conferred prior to the time of application, or ABD status with dissertation scheduled at the time of application. Conferral of doctoral degree by start date. Other Required Qualifications Master’s degree in Social Work and at least 2 years of post-master’s degree social work practice experience. Demonstrated potential for research and scholarship, teaching and advising, and extension and engagement activities, as NC State is a land-grant university that highly values extension and engagement. Clear research agenda and the ability to carry out an original research agenda that advances the field of social work. Strong commitment to excellence in teaching and advising. Excellent communication skills and collegiality. Demonstrated commitment to ethical,practice, research, and teaching. Preferred Qualifications PhD. in social work or a closely related field, conferred prior to the time of application. Expertise in one or more of these specialty areas: public health social work policy advocacy behavioral health workforce substance use disorders gerontology community organization or community-based participatory research environmental justice and/or disaster social work digital/online social work criminal justice school social work international/global social work rural social work advanced clinical practice Demonstrated leadership ability. Experience in developing programs, curricula, and course content, including for online courses. Demonstrated teaching experience across the curriculum at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Experience with collaboration and intercultural communication. Demonstrated potential for leading groups focused on social work education. Experience teaching across various formats (in person, hybrid, online). Demonstrated potential for obtaining external funding to support research and scholarship. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/18/2026 Anticipated Close Date 10/02/2026; if posting is still active we are accepting and reviewing applications. Special Instructions to Applicants Please include with your application the following documents: Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Contact Information for References 2-page Teaching Philosophy 2-page Research Statement Position Details Position Number 00112330 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 162701 - School of Social Work EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a master's degree in Social Work? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have at least two years of full-time social work practice experience? (Open Ended Question) * Do you already have a Ph.D. in social work or a closely related field? (Open Ended Question) * If you do not yet have a Ph.D., please enter your dissertation defense date. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for References Research Statement Teaching Statement Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/235132": {
      "title": "Asst./Assoc. Professor, ITAO",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Asst./Assoc. Professor, ITAO Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Asst./Assoc. Professor, ITAO Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include the following as part of your application: 1. Cover Letter 2. Resume/CV 3. Teaching Statement 4. Research Statement 5. Contact information for references Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194891EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Asst./Assoc. Professor, ITAO Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with Experience. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00 am - 5:00 pm (weekends and nights as needed) Job Location Raleigh, NC Department ITAO - Poole College of Management About the Department The Poole College of Management actively engages with industry and academia to create an innovative and collaborative intellectual environment that fosters learning, scholarship, and service. We’re deeply rooted in NC State’s history as a university that excels at science, technology, engineering, and math. Our college’s varied student body — over 4,500 students — hails from across North Carolina, the United States, and the world. Our faculty are thought leaders and field-tested experts with enduring ties to the world of business. Poole College of Management has six academic departments: Accounting; Economics; Finance; Information Technology, Analytics and Operations ( ITAO ); Marketing; Management, Innovation, and Entrepreneurship ( MIE ). We offer bachelor’s degrees in accounting, business administration, and economics; master’s degrees in accounting, business administration ( MBA ), economics, and management (including specialized degrees); as well as joint doctoral degrees in economics and operations research. Among our non-degree programs, we offer Executive Education and graduate certificates. The college houses six initiatives fostering research, learning, and corporate engagement: Business Analytics Initiative, Business Sustainability Collaborative, Enterprise Risk Management Initiative, Entrepreneurship Clinic, Entrepreneurship Collaborative, and Supply Chain Resource Cooperative. The college is fully accredited by the AACSB . To learn more about our College, visit: https://poole.ncsu.edu Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Information Technology, Analytics, and Operations in the Poole College of Management at North Carolina State University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. We seek collaborative and innovative scholars specializing in Operations and Supply Chain Management who demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in research, teaching, and service. Position Responsibilities Teaching : Deliver high-quality instruction in Operations and Supply Chain Management at both the undergraduate and graduate (including MBA ) levels, in online and in-person formats. Courses may include topics such as operations management, purchasing and supply management, logistics management, operations modeling and analysis, or supply chain management. Research : Develop and maintain a productive research program that leads to publications in top-tier peer-reviewed journals. Service : Contribute to the academic mission of the department, college, and university through committee work, curriculum development, and professional engagement. Perform other duties as assigned by the department head. Candidates must be a contributing faculty member to department and college service activities. If you are a collaborative, innovative scholar with a passion for research and teaching in operations and supply chain management, and are eager to contribute to a dynamic academic community, we encourage you to apply. Appointment Details The anticipated start date is August 16, 2027. Other Responsibilities Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Candidates must currently hold a Ph.D., or have completed the requirements for the degree by August 16, 2027, in Operations Management, Supply Chain Management, or a closely related field. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Other Required Qualifications Candidates should demonstrate research and teaching capabilities consistent with a Research 1 university, showing strong potential at the assistant professor level or an established record at the associate professor level, with the ability to teach effectively at both undergraduate and graduate levels. Preferred Qualifications Experience mentoring graduate and undergraduate students in research or projects. Familiarity with interdisciplinary research collaborations or industry partnerships. Proven track record of securing competitive research grants and funding. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/18/2026 Anticipated Close Date 11/1/2026; if posting is still active we are accepting and reviewing applications Special Instructions to Applicants Please include the following as part of your application: 1. Cover Letter 2. Resume/CV 3. Teaching Statement 4. Research Statement 5. Contact information for references Position Details Position Number 00112336 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.00 FTE Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 208001 - ITAO - Poole College of Management EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Research Statement Teaching Statement Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
