    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/235052": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Insect Ecology",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant Professor in Insect Ecology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant Professor in Insect Ecology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following: Cover letter CV Teaching philosophy Research statement Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194877EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant Professor in Insect Ecology Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with education and experience. Work Schedule Core Business Hours (Monday - Friday; 8:00 am - 5:00 pm) schedule will vary based on teaching and research needs. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Entomology and Plant Pathology About the Department As part of the Land Grant University, the Department of Entomology and Plant Pathology in the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences at North Carolina State University is composed of over 40 faculty that direct a diverse portfolio of programs in teaching, research, and extension. Collectively, these strengths serve our clientele and our science, providing a rich environment for graduate education and training that can be tailored to students’ career interests in basic and translational science or extension. Our education and research programs provide graduate and undergraduate students with unique hands-on learning opportunities using the latest technologies. Entomology and Plant Pathology houses the Structural Pest Management Training Facility, an Insect Museum with over 2 million vouchered insects, Plant Disease and Insect Clinic, the Larry Grand Mycological Herbarium, Micropropagation and Repository Unit, and the Center for Integrated Fungal Research. The College of Agriculture and Life Sciences houses 12 Academic departments with 294 faculty, 2,891 undergraduate students and 899 graduate students. The College is home to 18 research stations strategically located across the state that enhance our interactions with our farmers, stakeholders, and industry partners. Our strategic plan, Growing Our Future 2023-2030 is accessible here https://units.cals.ncsu.edu/cals-strategic-plan/. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Entomology and Plant Pathology invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Insect Ecology with 60% effort in teaching and mentoring and 40% effort in research and discovery. We seek a dynamic scholar committed to excellence in undergraduate and graduate education, student engagement, and innovative teaching, alongside development of an active, externally funded research program. The Assistant Professor will play a central role in the department’s undergraduate curriculum, including instruction of ENT 201: Insects and People , a high-enrollment course serving approximately 140 students in an in-person spring section and virtual sections offered in spring and fall. Additionally this role will contribute to additional undergraduate and graduate courses aligned with the faculty member’s expertise and departmental needs. In addition to teaching, you will have the opportunity to establish a nationally recognized research program broadly focused on insect ecology, with research spanning areas such as insect behavior, plant–insect interactions, community ecology, conservation, global change biology, or related fields. Your research program will attract competitive extramural support from federal agencies, foundations, industry, and other sources while providing meaningful research and professional-development opportunities for undergraduate, graduate, and postdoctoral students. Key Responsibilities: Teaching and Mentoring: Lead instruction for ENT 201: Insects and People , including in-person and distance-education formats, and teach additional undergraduate and graduate courses aligned with expertise and departmental needs. Develop and use innovative, accessible, and technology-enhanced instructional approaches while contributing to curriculum development, assessment, and continuous improvement. Mentor undergraduate, M.S., and Ph.D. students through research, experiential learning, and career development. Support student recruitment, retention, and success while contributing to departmental teaching initiatives. Research and Discovery: Develop and sustain an externally funded research program in insect ecology that complements and strengthens departmental expertise. Conduct impactful research that may integrate field-based ecological studies with molecular, computational, spatial, or other data-driven approaches, and maintain a strong record of peer-reviewed publications and scholarly productivity. Engage undergraduate and graduate students in research, providing meaningful training and mentorship. Collaborate with departmental, university, and external partners to advance research, teaching, and outreach goals. Service and Engagement: Contribute to departmental, college, university, and professional service through committee participation, faculty governance, scientific societies, and manuscript and grant review. Foster interdisciplinary collaborations and contribute to a collegial and productive academic environment. Engage in outreach that enhances the visibility and impact of the department and university. If you are an engaged educator and collaborative scholar who sees opportunities to connect insect ecology with the questions that matter to students, communities, and the broader scientific community, we invite you to join the Department of Entomology and Plant Pathology. Other Responsibilities In addition to the core responsibilities of this role, there may be occasional opportunities to take on additional duties. This offers an opportunity to build on your skills, explore new areas, and gain a deeper understanding of the department’s operations. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience PhD-equivalent degree in entomology, biology, ecology, evolutionary biology, or related field. Other Required Qualifications Demonstrated teaching experience at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Expertise in insect ecology, with specialization in one or more areas such as: Integrated pest management Invasive species and biological invasions Pollination biology and ecosystem services Vector ecology and disease systems Trophic interactions and food web dynamics Urban and managed ecosystems Climate change and global change biology Forest and conservation ecology Molecular, population, community, or ecosystem ecology Preferred Qualifications Record of research efforts supported by serving as PI, Co-PI or listed author on peer-reviewed publications. Required License(s) or Certification(s) Valid NC Driver’s License Valid NC Driver's License required Yes Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/16/2026 Anticipated Close Date 10/28/2026; if posting is active we are still accepting and reviewing applications Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following: Cover letter CV Teaching philosophy Research statement Position Details Position Number 00102456 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.00 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Mandatory - Medical Emergencies Department ID 111801 - Entomology and Plant Pathology EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have an NC Driver's License or the ability to obtain one within 60 days of hire? Yes No Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for References Research Statement Teaching Statement Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/235031": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Scholar",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. 1. Applicants should attach the following supporting documents to the application: Cover Letter (Letter of interest addressing the major job criteria) Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for References Two (2) Short Writing Samples (Preferably published in high-impact factor journals) Research Statement 2. Applicants must arrange to have two letters of recommendation sent to the attention of Dr. Dubljevic at the following email address: veljko_dubljevic@ncsu.edu . Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191772PD Position Number 00112325 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 160501 - Philosophy & Religious Studies Department 160501 - Philosophy & Religious Studies Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties The department of Philosophy and Religious Studies invites applications for a Postdoctoral Research Scholar in STS , empirical neuro ethics, or ethics of AI at the Neuro Computational Ethics Research Group, in the College of Humanities and Social Sciences, beginning January 2027 . Duties and Responsibilities Include: developing and experimentally testing VR simulations for moral decision making broadly promoting AI ethics scholarship The position entails a specific research agenda that aligns with activities described in Dr. Veljko Dubljevic’s NEH AI Center grant. Other Work/Responsibilities The successful candidate will also assist with scholarly publications on the ethics of Self-Driving Labs, teach one or two courses in AI Ethics and pursue a research agenda in this domain and other forms of AI and be guided by Dr. Dubljevic. A presentation given once per semester will summarize progress in this arena and should result in one or more scholarly publications. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Full-time; Workdays 9am - 5pm Department Required Skills Editorial work experience Excellent communication skills Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Doctoral project/dissertation that demonstrates ability to perform close readings of texts. Experience as instructor of record preferred (though experience as teaching assistant acceptable). Preference given to candidates who incorporate study of state-of-the-art research in AI ethics into their scholarship and/or teaching. Training/education: Experience mentoring undergraduate students desired. Motivation to teach, mentor, conduct and publish research and/or scholarship expected. Required License or Certification n/a Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $48,079 @ 9months If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 09/15/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/235030 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for References Short Writing Sample Research Statement Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
