    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234855": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Teaching Professor in Geospatial Analytics",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant/Associate Teaching Professor in Geospatial Analytics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant/Associate Teaching Professor in Geospatial Analytics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. As part of your application please include the following: 1. Curriculum Vitae 2. Cover Letter 3. Teaching Statement: (1-2 pages) Please describe your overall teaching philosophy and specifically how you approach teaching geospatial knowledge and technical skills. Please also discuss how your research and disciplinary background inform your approach to geospatial teaching in interdisciplinary programs, particularly when working with students from varied majors, academic backgrounds, and perspectives. 4. Teaching Portfolio (Other Document 1): include a sample syllabus from a GIS course you’ve developed and taught as instructor of record (if you have not served as Instructor of Record, a syllabus where you served as TA can be substituted) a table listing all courses taught as instructor of record, with GIS courses listed first; Include course title, level (undergraduate/graduate), delivery mode (online/in person/hybrid), number of times taught, and approximate number of students; If you have not been instructor of record, list all GIS courses you have served as a TA and your responsibilities in that course; a table listing the geospatial technologies you are familiar with and proficiency level (beginner, intermediate, expert). Note: References will be requested of finalists. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194853EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant/Associate Teaching Professor in Geospatial Analytics Anticipated Hiring Range Rank and salary commensurate with education and experience. Work Schedule Monday - Friday; 8:00 am - 5:00 pm Job Location Raleigh, NC Department The Center for Geospatial Analytics About the Department The Center for Geospatial Analytics ( CGA ) at North Carolina State University is a premier interdisciplinary hub dedicated to addressing grand challenges through spatial data science and geospatial analytics. The Center offers a vibrant research environment with access to state-of-the-art facilities, including the Geovisualization Lab, where we pioneer cutting-edge open source tools and geospatial approaches. By working across departmental boundaries—spanning computer science, engineering, natural resources, and the social sciences—staff and faculty engage in high-impact projects that range from ecological disease and wildfire ecology to urban growth and agricultural intelligence. Beyond its robust research portfolio and interdisciplinary network of affiliates, the Center is a recognized leader in geospatial education, offering a collaborative ecosystem that supports professional growth, innovation, and academic excellence. The Center’s academic programs, including the unique Ph.D. in Geospatial Analytics, Graduate Certificate in GIS , the top-ranked professional Master’s in Geospatial Information Science and Technology ( MGIST ) and undergraduate minor in Geospatial Analytics, are designed to train the next generation of interdisciplinary data scientists and geospatial professionals. At CGA , students and researchers do more than analyze data; they apply geospatial thinking to address pressing environmental and societal challenges. The Center fosters a culture grounded in mentorship, collaboration, and the practical application of theory to real-world problems. By bridging foundational geographic theory, advanced visualization technologies, and community-engaged research, CGA creates an environment where innovation and impact go hand in hand. This commitment to academic rigor, interdisciplinary collaboration, and public impact makes the Center for Geospatial Analytics an ideal destination for professionals seeking a forward-thinking, inclusive, and impact-driven workplace. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Center for Geospatial Analytics is seeking a highly qualified instructor to join our academic programs at the rank of Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor (non-tenure). The candidates we are seeking are forward-looking instructors with a strong background in both foundational geospatial concepts and skills alongside modern approaches, such as open-source and cloud-based/native platforms, WebGIS, GeoAI, Geospatial Data Science, and a strong interest in innovative geospatial pedagogy and dedication to student success. This is a full-time, 9-month professional track faculty position with an initial contract of three (3) years, with opportunities for multiple renewals and advancement based on annual performance reviews and progress. The Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor will play an instrumental role in developing and delivering high-quality courses for the Center’s highly-ranked academic programs. In this role, you will shape students’ learning experiences through 15–18 credit hours of teaching each academic year across the Fall and Spring terms. You will teach courses within the existing curriculum while also having the opportunity to develop new courses that reflect your expertise, interests, and emerging needs in the field of geospatial analytics. Teaching responsibilities will include: An undergraduate- or graduate-level introductory GIS course (3 credit hours) The undergraduate Minor Capstone Course, Geospatial Analytics in Practice (1 credit hour; Fall and Spring) Two additional undergraduate courses, or a combination of undergraduate and graduate courses, based on program needs and the candidate’s interests. Potential topics for new courses include, but are not limited to, Geospatial AI, Geospatial Ethics, AI and Data Literacy in GIS , Environmental/Public Health/Hydrological Applications, and Geospatial Communication and Cartography. Service and engagement responsibilities include: Participation in the Center’s academic community through student advising and mentoring, including serving as an academic advisor for a portion of MGIST students Participation in committees in support of program-level initiatives and outreach, as requested If you enjoy connecting technical geospatial concepts to practical applications, communicating clearly with students, and collaborating with colleagues to develop and strengthen courses, we encourage you to apply. Other Responsibilities n/a Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience PhD in GIS , Geospatial Science, Geospatial Analytics, Computational Geography, Remote Sensing, Planning, or a closely related field with demonstrated teaching experience at the university level. Additionally, for consideration at the Associate Teaching Professor level, a minimum of 5 years of geospatial/ GIS -related teaching experience at the undergraduate and/or graduate levels. Other Required Qualifications Experience teaching at least one university-level course in GIS or a closely related field Proficiency in GIS technologies (ArcGIS Pro/Enterprise, ArcGIS Online, QGIS , etc.) Demonstrated experience working with geospatial data and analytical workflows Familiarity with computational and/or scripting approaches used in GIS (e.g., Arcade, Python, R, SQL , JavaScript) Ability to design aligned course components, including learning objectives, assignments, and assessments that clearly support student learning outcomes Familiarity with AI platforms used in instruction (i.e., Google Gemini, Notebook LM, ChatGPT) and geospatial-specific AI tools (ArcGIS AI Assistants, QGIS AI, etc.) Ability to communicate complex geospatial concepts clearly to students and effectively collaborates with colleagues across the Center Preferred Qualifications Two or more years of university-level teaching experience as instructor of record, including at least one undergraduate- or graduate-level GIS course Background teaching students in online, synchronous, and/or asynchronous settings, with the ability to support student learning in large-enrollment courses Course development skills, with an interest in creating new courses and strengthening the Center’s evolving curriculum Experience with Open Source GIS platforms ( GRASS , QGIS , etc.) Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/11/2026 Anticipated Close Date 10/15/2026: if posting is active we are still accepting and reviewing applications. Special Instructions to Applicants As part of your application please include the following: 1. Curriculum Vitae 2. Cover Letter 3. Teaching Statement: (1-2 pages) Please describe your overall teaching philosophy and specifically how you approach teaching geospatial knowledge and technical skills. Please also discuss how your research and disciplinary background inform your approach to geospatial teaching in interdisciplinary programs, particularly when working with students from varied majors, academic backgrounds, and perspectives. 4. Teaching Portfolio (Other Document 1): include a sample syllabus from a GIS course you’ve developed and taught as instructor of record (if you have not served as Instructor of Record, a syllabus where you served as TA can be substituted) a table listing all courses taught as instructor of record, with GIS courses listed first; Include course title, level (undergraduate/graduate), delivery mode (online/in person/hybrid), number of times taught, and approximate number of students; If you have not been instructor of record, list all GIS courses you have served as a TA and your responsibilities in that course; a table listing the geospatial technologies you are familiar with and proficiency level (beginner, intermediate, expert). Note: References will be requested of finalists. Position Details Position Number 00112301 Position Type Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 150103 - The Center for Geospatial Analytics EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Describe how your area of geospatial expertise could contribute to the education of undergraduate and graduate students in geospatial analytics at NC State. (Open Ended Question) * Briefly describe your approach to integrating AI tools to support student learning (Open Ended Question) * How do you see Geospatial education evolving over the next 5 years? (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Other Document (1) Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234851": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Scholar",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191770PD Position Number 00112322 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 140801 - Materials Science &Engineering Department 140801 - Materials Science &Engineering Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties The Department of Materials Science and Engineering ( MSE ) at NC State University is a nationally recognized leader in materials discovery, design and deployment. Our faculty, students and staff work at the forefront of innovation: advancing materials that enable breakthroughs in energy, electronics, health, manufacturing and sustainability. Research in MSE spans theory, computation, synthesis, characterization and scale-up, supported by a collaborative culture and state-of-the-art facilities on NC State’s Centennial Campus. Faculty lead internationally visible efforts in areas such as artificial intelligence-driven materials design, wide bandgap semiconductors, energy storage, nanomaterials, soft and biomaterials and structural materials under extreme environments. Representative labs include: Atomic-Scale Materials Lab Wide Bandgap Semiconductor Lab AIMS Lab Corrosion and Advanced Materials Lab Augustyn Research Lab Learn how NC State MSE is leading the way to discover, create and enhance the world around us. Primary duties and responsibilities of this position include: Machine Learning Model Development : Design, implement, and optimize machine learning algorithms to enhance or develop new force fields for molecular simulations. Focus on leveraging modern techniques such as neural networks, Gaussian processes, and transfer learning to improve predictive accuracy and computational efficiency. Data Analysis & Preprocessing : Gather and preprocess large-scale simulation and experimental data. Identify key features, perform dimensionality reduction, and ensure the data is properly formatted for training machine learning models. Simulation & Benchmarking : Conduct molecular dynamics and quantum mechanical simulations to generate training and validation datasets. Benchmark newly developed models against existing force fields and experimental results to assess performance and reliability. Collaboration & Publication : Work closely with interdisciplinary teams of computational chemists, materials scientists, and biophysicists to apply machine learning models to a variety of systems. Publish results in high-impact journals and present findings at relevant conferences. Software Development & Documentation : Contribute to the development of open-source software tools and frameworks for machine learning-based force field modeling. Ensure thorough documentation and reproducibility of all work. Mentorship : Mentor graduate students and junior researchers in computational techniques, machine learning methodologies, and scientific writing. Other Work/Responsibilities Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule M-F, 8:00AM-5:00PM Department Required Skills NA Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education A Ph.D. in Materials Science and Engineering, Computer Science and Engineering, or a related discipline. Strong expertise in data science techniques, demonstrating ability in their application to materials research. Creativity and a proactive approach to problem-solving. Excellent communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively within a diverse multidisciplinary team. Required License or Certification NA Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $58,656-$60,000 If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 09/10/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234850 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU website Craigslist Indeed.com Carolina Job Finder/Employment Guide NC Works Dress for Success Technical/Trade School Program Job Fair (Identify Job Fair in question #2 below) Direct Contact from NSCU Representative (identify person in question #2 below) Other Monster.com Other online job board NCSU employee referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Ohter) If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Contact Information for References Optional Documents Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation 1 NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
