    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234580": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Scholar",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191766PD Position Number 00112313 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 147501 - Lampe Joint Department of BME Department 147501 - Lampe Joint Department of BME Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties The Atcha Lab based at NC State is seeking a highly motivated postdoctoral scholar to investigate how mechanical and biochemical cues regulate cell-cell interactions during cardiovascular disease. The lab combines mechanobiology, biomaterials, and molecular biology to uncover mechanisms of cardiac disease and identify new therapeutic targets. Other Work/Responsibilities Postdoctoral research scholar will form and conduct their own independent research projects and will support undergraduate and graduate students. They will also contribute in the writing of grant proposals and will present findings at research conferences. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Mon-Fri 8-5 or as required by supervisor Department Required Skills Strong experience in molecular biology techniques (Westernblot, ELISA , qPCR, immunofluorescence, etc.) Experience using statistical analysis software (R, Prism, MATLAB , etc.) Experience in analyzing RNA -seq and Single Cell RNA -seqdata sets Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong analytical, organizational, and project management abilities. Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with interdisciplinary teams and external partners. Ability to communicate complex research findings to academic and practitioner audiences. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Experience in ion channel pathophysiology Experience in engineering design and fabrication Required License or Certification n/a Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $62,000 - $64,000 If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 09/02/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234578 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Contact Information for References Resume/CV Optional Documents Cover Letter NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
