    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234438": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Scholar",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach a CV/resume, cover letter, contact information for three references Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191763PD Position Number 00112280 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 140201 - Chemical & Biomolecular Engineering Department 140201 - Chemical & Biomolecular Engineering Job City & State Raleigh, North Carolina Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties The Abolhasani Research Group in the Department of Chemical & Biomolecular Engineering at North Carolina State University is seeking a Postdoctoral Research Scholar to develop next-generation self-driving laboratories and autonomous experimentation technologies as part of the NSF -funded SPEED (Self-driving Platforms for Expedited Experimental co-Design) Programmable Cloud Laboratory. The successful candidate will develop and deploy closed-loop experimental platforms that integrate automated synthesis and experimentation, real-time characterization, data analysis, and AI/ML-based experiment selection. The research will focus on creating modular, reliable, and user-accessible autonomous laboratories for accelerated discovery and optimization in chemistry and materials science. Highly motivated candidates with experience in laboratory automation, autonomous experimentation, robotics, scientific instrumentation, process control, or related areas are encouraged to apply. Experience with Python-based automation and integration of laboratory hardware and analytical instruments is highly desirable. The successful candidate will work in a highly interdisciplinary environment involving chemical engineers, chemists, materials scientists, computer scientists, AI/ML researchers, and external academic and industrial partners. Duties and Responsibilities include: Design, develop, and deploy self-driving laboratory platforms for autonomous chemical and materials experimentation. Integrate synthesis, sample handling, analytical characterization, and data-processing tools into automated experimental workflows. Develop Python-based interfaces for laboratory hardware and scientific instruments. Implement closed-loop workflows connecting experimental platforms with AI/ML experiment-selection algorithms. Develop methods for automated calibration, fault detection, error recovery, and experimental quality control. Establish standardized workflows and interfaces that allow experimental platforms to be used by external SPEED users. Conduct autonomous and high-throughput experimental campaigns. Analyze experimental data and evaluate the performance and robustness of autonomous workflows. Collaborate with SPEED researchers in chemistry, materials science, AI/ML, data science, and automation. Prepare manuscripts, presentations, technical documentation, and regular project reports. Meet regularly with the PI and SPEED team to review progress, milestones, and future research plans. Other Work/Responsibilities Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday-Friday 8am-5pm Department Required Skills Demonstrated experience in experimental research, laboratory automation, robotics, process control, scientific instrumentation, or related areas. Ability to work effectively in a multidisciplinary research environment. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Experience with Python, laboratory automation, robotic systems, instrument APIs, process control, automated characterization, data acquisition, high-throughput experimentation, or self-driving laboratories is preferred. Experience integrating multiple instruments into end-to-end automated experimental workflows is particularly desirable. Required License or Certification N/A Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $61,000-$64,000 If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 08/31/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234437 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
