    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234375": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor and Extension Specialist in Row Crop Entomology",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant Professor and Extension Specialist in Row Crop Entomology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant Professor and Extension Specialist in Row Crop Entomology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include the following as a part of your application packet. 1. CV 2. Cover Letter 3. Research Statement (2 page max) 4. Extension Statement (Other document 1) (2 page max) 5. Contact information for References Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194828EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant Professor and Extension Specialist in Row Crop Entomology Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with Experience ($85,000 - $97,000) Work Schedule Core Business Hours (Monday - Friday; 8:00 am - 5:00 pm) schedule will vary based on extension and research needs. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Entomology and Plant Pathology About the Department As part of the Land Grant University, the Department of Entomology and Plant Pathology in the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences at North Carolina State University is composed of over 40 faculty that direct a diverse portfolio of programs in teaching, research, and extension. Collectively, these strengths not only serve our clientele and our science but also provide a rich environment for graduate education and training that can be tailored to the specific career interests of the student, irrespective of whether they prefer training in the basic sciences or are preparing for a career in extension. Our education and research programs provide graduate and undergraduate students with unique hands-on learning opportunities using the latest technologies. Entomology and Plant Pathology houses the Plant Disease and Insect Clinic, the Larry Grand Mycological Herbarium, Micropropagation and Repository Unit, Structural Pest Management Training Facility, an Insect Museum with 1.9 million vouchered insects, and the Center for Integrated Fungal Research. The College of Agriculture and Life Sciences houses 12 Academic departments with 294faculty, 2,891 undergraduate students and 899 graduate students. The College is home to 18 research stations strategically located across the state that enhances our interactions with our farmers, stakeholders, and industry partners. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Entomology and Plant Pathology seeks a tenure-track Assistant Professor (12-month) to provide statewide leadership in arthropod management for North Carolina row crop production, with a focus on sweetpotato, peanut, and soybean. The position is 70% Extension and 30% research , connecting applied research, grower needs, and emerging technologies to strengthen sustainable pest management across North Carolina agriculture. You’ll have the opportunity to build on your expertise in row crop entomology, integrated pest management, pest ecology, and insecticide resistance while shaping innovative approaches to pest prediction, decision support, and resistance management. Your work may draw on field experimentation, landscape-scale studies, pest monitoring, and data-driven tools, including artificial intelligence, precision agriculture, remote sensing, and drones. Through your research and Extension program, you’ll translate new knowledge into practical solutions that help growers and agricultural professionals make informed, sustainable pest management decisions. Key responsibilities fall within the following functional areas. Extension & Outreach: Shape a statewide Extension program that helps North Carolina growers address arthropod pest challenges in major row crops, including sweetpotato, peanut, and soybean. Translate research into practical recommendations that help growers, consultants, and industry stakeholders make informed pest management decisions. Connect with agricultural professionals and growers through field days, Extension programming, and innovative digital decision-support tools. Build strong partnerships with commodity groups, Extension agents, and state and federal partners to address emerging arthropod management challenges. Support the growth and development of graduate students and other trainees through mentorship, research guidance, and professional development opportunities. Strengthen agricultural workforce capacity by developing training and professional development opportunities for Extension agents, consultants, and agricultural professionals. Advance adoption of integrated pest management through innovative technologies and decision-support tools that translate research into practical solutions for North Carolina agriculture. Research & Discovery: Build an applied, externally funded research program that responds to grower needs and strengthens the impact of your Extension work. Advance understanding of pest ecology and management through field- and landscape-scale research addressing current and emerging crop protection challenges. Share new knowledge and practical solutions through peer-reviewed publications, Extension resources, and other scholarly contributions. Secure and steward extramural funding to advance applied research and strengthen the impact of Extension priorities. Mentorship, Teaching & Service: Mentor graduate students and other trainees through research guidance, professional development, and career preparation. Contribute to undergraduate and graduate instruction through teaching courses and supporting the department’s educational mission. Contribute expertise and perspective through departmental, college, university, and professional service activities. If you are a collaborative entomologist who enjoys connecting research with real-world agricultural challenges, building strong relationships with growers and partners, and developing innovative solutions for sustainable crop protection, we encourage you to apply. Other Responsibilities In addition to the core responsibilities of this role, there will be occasional opportunities to take on additional duties. This offers an opportunity to build on your skills, explore new areas, and gain a deeper understanding of the department, college and university operations. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience PhD in entomology or equivalent degree Other Required Qualifications Knowledge of integrated pest management ( IPM ) principles and their application to agronomic cropping systems. Expertise in pest ecology and management across field, landscape, and broader agroecosystem scales. Advanced understanding of insecticide resistance mechanisms and proven capability in developing and applying innovative resistance management strategies. Technical experience with AI, precision agriculture, remote sensing, drones, or other emerging technologies applied to crop protection. Preferred Qualifications Extension experience in Row Crop Entomology Required License(s) or Certification(s) NC Pesticide License NC Driver’s License Valid NC Driver's License required Yes Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 08/28/2026 Anticipated Close Date 12/1/2026; if posting is still active we are still accepting and reviewing applications Special Instructions to Applicants Please include the following as a part of your application packet. 1. CV 2. Cover Letter 3. Research Statement (2 page max) 4. Extension Statement (Other document 1) (2 page max) 5. Contact information for References Position Details Position Number 00105789 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.00 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 111801 - Entomology and Plant Pathology EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a valid North Carolina Pesticide license or the ability to obtain one within three months of employment? Yes No * Do you, or will you, have a valid NC Driver's license or the ability to obtain one within 60 days of hire? Yes No * Do you have (or will you have by date of hire) a PhD in Entomology or field related to the job description? Yes No * Please describe your experience (if any) leveraging geospatial data for use in agriculture or other environment. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your experience (if any) interacting with stakeholders in an extension or outreach context. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your mentorship experience(s). (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Other Document (1) Contact Information for References Research Statement Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234360": {
      "title": "Educational Postdoctoral Research Scholar",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Educational Postdoctoral Research Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Educational Postdoctoral Research Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191761PD Position Number 00112298 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 195001 - Department of Clinical Sciences Department 195001 - Department of Clinical Sciences Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties This Educational Postdoctoral Research Scholar is designed to bridge the gap between clinical expertise and educational scholarship. By combining research training with hands-on teaching experience, the Postdoctoral Research Scholar will develop the skills necessary to become a leader in veterinary education and communication and professional pedagogy. Program Overview: Duration: 12-24 months Primary Objective: To equip DVM or PhD professionals with the methodological toolkit required to conduct high-impact research in health communication, communication and educational theory, and professionalism/professional identity. Eligibility & Qualifications : Must hold a DVM (or equivalent) or a PhD in a related field (Education, Communication, Psychology, etc.). Research & Methodological Training: The Postdoctoral Research Scholar will participate in a structured mentorship program to master mixed-methods research tailored to the veterinary healthcare and educational environment. Responsibilities include: Quantitative research methodologies, including survey design, statistical analysis of educational outcomes (such as competency-based assessments), and data-driven evaluation of communication interventions Qualitative research methods, including thematic analysis of reflective practice, conducting and coding focus groups and semi-structured interviews, and utilizing ethnographic or observational approaches Scholarly output through writing and submitting one first-author manuscript per year to a peer-reviewed journal (e.g., Journal of Veterinary Medical Education ) Teaching, Facilitation, and Curriculum: The Postdoctoral Research Scholar will be integrated into the DVM curriculum to ground ongoing research initiatives in active educational practice related to professionalism and communication training. Responsibilities Include: Communication Lab Facilitation - Leading small-group sessions using simulated clients (SCs) and providing real-time, constructive feedback to DVM students on clinical communication Guest Lecturing – Developing and delivering didactic content on topics such as conflict management, breaking bad news, or veterinary professional ethics Curriculum Development – Collaborating with faculty to refine and enhance learning modules and assessments across the professionalism curriculum Other Work/Responsibilities Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00am to 5:00pm Department Required Skills N/A Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education • A demonstrated passion for veterinary pedagogy, communication, and the evolution of professional identity and professionalism. • Strong interpersonal skills, a collaborative mindset, and a desire to transition into an academic or leadership role. Required License or Certification N/A Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $58,656 - $60,000 If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 08/28/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234359 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
