    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/233526": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Scholar",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach a Cover Letter, resume/CV, and contact information for three (3) professional references. Please make sure that the information entered on the application matches what is on your resume. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191618PD Position Number 00111863 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 110901 - Crop and Soil Sciences Department 110901 - Crop and Soil Sciences Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties The Department of Crop and Soil Sciences encompasses varied disciplines in research, extension, and teaching. The department’s mission is to develop future leaders in crop, soil and environmental sciences, improve crop plants and products, devise effective and sustainable crop production systems, devise effective and sustainable soil management techniques in both agriculture and urban settings; and disseminate crop, soil, and environmental science, knowledge for the benefit of producers of food, feed, turf, biofuels and fiber in North Carolina. Duties and Responsibilities: The primary responsibilities of this position are to conduct, perform, and execute cotton genetics and breeding research focused on genomic selection (GS), nested association mapping ( NAM ), and genome-wide association studies ( GWAS ) for important agronomic traits in tetraploid cotton. The candidate is expected to perform cotton genetics and breeding research in the field, greenhouse, and lab-based settings; develop and evaluate genetic, genomic resources, and analysis of genotypic data ( GBS , resequencing, array-based and targeted genotyping panel SNPs) and phenotypic data, and use a varied array of statistical, genetics, and bioinformatics tools and methods. This position requires the candidate to summarize results, present them as technical reports and presentations at the meetings, and communicate through peer-reviewed publications. The candidate will have the opportunity to participate and cooperatively work with other lab members in the ongoing trait mapping and breeding projects towards dissecting the genetic architecture of agronomic traits and improving cotton productivity through advanced breeding tools. Further, the candidate is expected to mentor and supervise the students in the cotton program. This position is initially for one year but can be extended based on satisfactory research progress and availability of funds. Other Work/Responsibilities The Postdoc researcher is expected to mentor and manage student researchers in all settings of the cotton genetics and breeding program (lab, greenhouse, and field-based). The Postdoc is expected to effectively manage the cotton genetic resources in the greenhouses and in the field, and seed processing, storage, and organization of seed. The Postdoc researcher is expected to cooperatively work with a varied group of cotton scientists across the US cotton belt in collecting and analyzing data and communicating the research results to peer reviewed manuscripts. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8 am - 5 pm Department Required Skills PhD in genetics or, plant breeding or plant biology, or related field. Computer-literate. Excellent oral and written communication skills and the ability to work well independently and in a collaborative research environment are essential. Prior experience in field breeding of cotton, including experimental design, planting, sampling, and data collection. Prior experience with phenotypic and genotypic data analysis is required. Experience with statistical analyses using SAS and/or R programs in plant breeding is required. Experience in communication of research results in peer-reviewed journals is required. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Experience in molecular genetic analysis of complex plant traits is preferred. Required License or Certification A valid NC Driver’s License and the ability to obtain an NC Driver’s License within 60 days of hire. A valid Driver’s License must be maintained throughout employment. Valid NC Driver's License required? Yes Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range commensurate with experience ($58,656) If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 08/04/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/227324 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Contact Information for References Resume/CV Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/233144": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Scholar - DEPP",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar - DEPP Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar - DEPP Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191742PD Position Number 00109651 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 111801 - Entomology and Plant Pathology Department 111801 - Entomology and Plant Pathology Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties We seek a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Scholar to conduct research in nematode genomics and molecular plant-nematode interactions. The position will focus on both basic and translational research aimed at understanding root-knot nematode ( RKN ) virulence, host adaptation, and mechanisms associated with resistance breaking in crops. The major focus of the project will be characterizing virulence-associated genes in M. enterolobii and investigating their interactions with crop hosts, including sweet potato. Additional projects will involve the integration of multi-omics datasets to better understand RKN -hosts interactions. The postdoc scholar will lead both laboratory experiments and computational analyses. The work will combine molecular biology, nematology, genomics, bioinformatics, and comparative transcriptomics. Depending on research interests and project needs, the successful candidate may also contribute to functional characterization of candidate nematode genes and host- resistant associated genes. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to work closely with collaborators at NC State University and other institutions Duties and Responsibilities: Conduct laboratory and greenhouse experiments related to plant-nematode interactions, nematode virulence, and host resistance Perform molecular biology experiments, including DNA and RNA extractions, PCR , qPCR, preparation of samples for genomics and transcriptomics analyses Conduct bioinformatics analyses using high-performance computing environments Maintain clear research records and contribute to reproducible bioinformatics workflows Other Work/Responsibilities In addition, Postdoctoral Research Scholar will: Mentor graduate and undergraduate students Lead the preparation of peer-reviewed manuscripts and contribute to grant proposals Present research findings at national and international scientific meetings Work collaboratively with researchers in the laboratory and with collaborators across NC State University and other institutions Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8am - 5pm Department Required Skills General knowledge of plants and pathogens including nematodes Ability to clearly and concisely present scientific data both orally and in writing Ability to design experiment, conduct independent research, and lead the preparation of manuscripts Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education The ideal candidate will have Ph.D. in plant pathology,nematology, molecular biology, plant biology, genomics andbioinformatics, or a closely related field Experience studying plant-pathogen interactions, plant-nematodeinteractions, or related host-microbe systems is preferred Experience with molecular biology techniques is desirable Experience using bioinformatics tools, and analyzing RNA -Seq, genomics, or other high-throughput sequencing datasets is strongly preferred A strong publication record appropriate to the candidate’s career stage is highly desirable Candidates should have strong scientific writing, data interpretation, communication skills, and an ability to work both independently and collaboratively Candidate should be a highly motivated and curious scientist with a strong interest in advancing research on plant-nematode interactions Required License or Certification N/A Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $59,000 - $62,000 If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 07/24/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/233143 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Contact Information for References Resume/CV Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/232982": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Scholar- Bioelectricity Lab",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar- Bioelectricity Lab Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar- Bioelectricity Lab Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191737PD Position Number 00112201 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 194001 - Department of Molecular Biomedical Sciences Department 194001 - Department of Molecular Biomedical Sciences Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties The Department of Molecular Biomedical Sciences trains doctors of veterinary medicine, graduate students, and postdoctoral fellows interested in research-based careers focused on discovering new information about animal and human health and disease and using those findings to enhance animal and human health and well-being. The Bioelectricity Lab develops next generation technologies for the detection and treatment of diseases using electric field mediated phenomena. Duties and Responsibilities: The candidate for the Bioelectricity Postdoc Research Scholar position will lead large/small animal studies investigating the immunological effects a new pulsed electric field cancer therapy. The candidate will additionally lead with other experiments in the laboratory using in vitro models to investigate the effects of pulsed electric fields on biological tissues. Other Work/Responsibilities Plan and conduct in vitro and small animal studies Evaluate samples from an participate in large animal studies Participate in lab meetings and journal club Prepare manuscripts and grants Other duties as assigned Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday-Friday, 8am-5pm with flexibility based on clinical schedules, animal/patient/experimental needs, and deadlines Department Required Skills ● Biological wet lab skills ● Small animal handling skills ● Writing manuscripts and grants Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Ph.D. with experience with pulsed electric field technologies Required License or Certification N/A Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $60,000-$75,000 If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many 2 Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 07/21/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/232980 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Pol