    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/227722": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Lecturer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Lecturer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include as attachments a resume/CV, cover letter, and contact information for at least 3 professional references. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194504EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Lecturer Anticipated Hiring Range $5,063 - $5,500 per course (depending on degree attained) Work Schedule Varies based on teaching schedule Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Department of Communication About the Department The Department of Communication is one of the largest departments in the College of Humanities and Social Sciences at NC State, with over 700 undergraduate majors and about 70 full- or part-time graduate students (M.S. and Ph.D.). We have two graduate programs: a Masters of Science in Communication and an interdisciplinary PhD program in Communication, Rhetoric and Digital Media in partnership with the Department of English. The Department of Communication at NC State is an accomplished community of students, staff members, teachers, and researchers with varied intellectual interests in the communication arts and sciences. Through our teaching, research and service, we cultivate responsible, caring and collaborative communication practices for our students, our community partners and the global citizenry. We do this because communication is central to addressing the significant challenges and opportunities of the 21st Century and we are committed to enabling people, organizations and communities to thrive. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Communication at North Carolina State University (NC State) invites applications for part-time Lecturer positions. Multiple hires may be made from this posting, with most positions being part-time and requiring in-person instruction. The position(s) are one-semester or one-year, non-tenure-track appointments with the possibility of renewal. Primary responsibilities include teaching undergraduate courses in communication as well as coordinating, planning, preparing, delivering, and evaluating classroom instruction and related activities. Other duties may be negotiated with the department head. Other Responsibilities Other tasks and responsibilities may be assigned based on the needs of the organization and evolving priorities. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Requires master’s degree, an equivalent degree, or equivalent professional experience. Other Required Qualifications Commitment to teaching excellence. Excellent communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience in communication at the college level and demonstrated teaching excellence. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's 