    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236598": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Biophilic Nature-Connected Urbanism",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Scholar - Biophilic Nature-Connected Urbanism Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Scholar - Biophilic Nature-Connected Urbanism Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Postdoc Submission requirements: 1. Curriculum vitae or resume 2. Cover letter describing research interests and their relationship to the position 3. Contact information for three professional references. *Applicants must meet NC State University eligibility requirements for appointment as a Postdoctoral Research Scholar. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191796PD Position Number 00111548 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 120401 - Landscape Architecture Department 120401 - Landscape Architecture Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties The Natural Learning Initiative seeks a postdoctoral research scholar to advance the emerging interdisciplinary field of biophilic nature-connected urbanism: the planning, design, programming, research, and stewardship of interconnected urban green infrastructure that integrates ecological and human developmental systems, enabling meaningful relationships with nature across the life course and generations. Nature-based Solutions (NbS) provide a global framework, supported by international treaties and policy commitments, including the UN Convention on the Rights of the Child, the UN Sustainable Development Goals, and the Social Determinants of Health. The position builds on NLI’s longstanding record of environment and behavior research and measurement; cross-sector professional development; learning resource production; evidence-based playful learning landscape design; universal co-design; and environmental quality assessment. The underlying premise is that regenerating biodiverse, interconnected urban green infrastructure, although essential, is insufficient to sustain a healthy planet. Urban environments must also enable people to experience, engage with, enjoy, understand, and care for nature in everyday life. For nature connectedness to become embedded in individual identity and transmitted across generations, experiences of nature must begin in early childhood and continue throughout life. Accordingly, early childhood facility naturalization and associated systems change remain a primary NLI focus. A central research proposition is that nature connectedness develops through networks of everyday settings repeatedly experienced across the life course—including homes, neighborhoods, childcare facilities, schools, parks, greenways, urban forests, campuses, workplaces, and civic landscapes. Together, these settings constitute developmental green infrastructure, supporting ecological functions while nurturing lifelong, intergenerational relationships with nature, expressed through arts, science, and community engagement embedded in nature-connected urban networks. In other words, urban landscapes must be planned, designed, managed, programmed, and assessed as ecological systems integrating nature and human development, inspiring cultural expression, to ensure intergenerational nature connectedness. Postdoc major responsibilities may include: Conduct literature reviews and synthesize research from relevant disciplines. Develop conceptual frameworks, research methods, measures, indicators, protocols, and measurement tools. Analyze existing NLI environmental assessment, behavior-mapping, observational, survey, and post-occupancy datasets. Design and conduct pilot field investigations across everyday socio-cultural physical environments. Investigate ecological, spatial, experiential, developmental, and intergenerational dimensions of nature connectedness. Prepare coauthored peer-reviewed publications, conference papers, research briefs, and professional publications. Contribute to research proposals and external funding opportunities. Collaborate with the NLI communications team on videos, animations, podcasts, diagrams, infographics, webinars, and other audiovisual and public-facing communication. Develop collaborations across NC State and with national and international research and practice partners. The successful candidate will have the opportunity not only to conduct research but to help define, test, measure, communicate, and establish biophilic nature-connected urbanism as an emerging field of research and practice contributing to a nature-connected society. If these works resonate, please apply for this unique position! NC State University NC State University, an R1 research institution, is located in the high-tech Research Triangle, alongside UNC -Chapel Hill and Duke University, in one of the fastest-growing regions in the U.S. Raleigh is reputed to be a low-stress place to live. NC State supports a high level of research activity and extensive doctoral programs. As the state’s flagship land-grant institution, research tends to focus on impactful, real-world solutions, driven by innovations and collaborations that address global challenges. The university consistently ranks among the top institutions in the country for research expenditures and technology commercialization. The Natural Learning Initiative The Natural Learning Initiative ( NLI ), based in the College of Design at NC State University (a land-grant R1 doctoral institution), advances research, design, professional development, and policy supporting environments for healthy human development and a healthy biosphere. NLI works across childcare, schools, parks, neighborhoods, communities, civic spaces, and other everyday environments to create equitable opportunities for engagement with nature. NLI was co-founded in 2000 by Robin Moore, architect and urban designer, Professor Emeritus of Landscape Architecture and Environmental Planning, Honorary ASLA ; and Research Professor Nilda Cosco, PhD, ASLA , NLI Director of Programs. Soolyeon Cho, PhD, is NLI Interim Director. Other Work/Responsibilities Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday-Friday 8am-5pm with option of 1 day/week remote work Department Required Skills Department Required Skills: PhD or equivalent degree in landscape architecture, landscape/environmental design, urban design, urban planning, horticultural science, environmental psychology, environmental education, child development, public health, urban ecology, geography, sustainability science, or a closely related field. A prior degree in landscape architecture, architecture, urban design, landscape design or similar built environment design degree. Demonstrated ability to conduct independent and collaborative research. Strong scholarly writing, analytical, and communication skills. Experience with quantitative, qualitative, or mixed research methods. Ability to work effectively across disciplinary and professional boundaries. Interest in human—environment relationships and translating research into design, practice, policy, and public communication. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Ph.D. or equivalent doctorate (e.g., DDes – Doctor of Design) in an appropriate filed awarded no more than five (5) years from the initial date of postdoctoral appointment. Preference will be given to candidates demonstrating one or more of the following: Peer-reviewed publication experience. Literature review and research synthesis. Environmental assessment, observational research, behavior mapping, surveys, spatial analysis, GIS , or statistical analysis. Research related to nature connectedness, biophilic design, children’s environments, public health, urban ecology, green infrastructure, or nature-based solutions. Development or validation or research measures and assessment tools. Field-based environmental or human-behavior research. Grant writing or collaborative proposal development. Communication of research through audiovisual, graphic, digital, or other public-facing media. Expertise in all areas is not expected . NLI seeks a scholar with strong research capabilities, intellectual curiosity, and enthusiasm for helping build an innovative interdisciplinary field framed by urban human development and nature connectedness. Required License or Certification N/A Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $60,000 If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 10/19/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236416 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Contact Information for References Resume/CV Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236596": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in LAEP &amp; Associate Director of NLI",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Associate Professor in LAEP &amp; Associate Director of NLI Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Associate Professor in LAEP & Associate Director of NLI Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants are required to submit: Letter of Intent (LOI) describing qualifications and interests, may be submitted under \"Cover Letter.\" CV (Curriculum Vitae) Digital portfolio or portfolio link via online application. *Note: digital portfolios and research publications may be submitted as \"Other Documents.\" List of references and their contact information Do not submit these materials via email. Email inquiries and nominations to the search committee co-chair, Dr. Nilda Cosco, at ngcosco@ncsu.edu Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194985EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Associate Professor in LAEP & Associate Director of NLI Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate based on experience Work Schedule Varies depending on project timelines and semester schedules. Evenings/weekends may be needed occasionally. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Landscape Architecture About the Department Landscape Architecture & Environmental Planning The Department of Landscape Architecture & Environmental Planning at NC State University is a nationally recognized leader in landscape architecture education, with a strong track record of ASLA national recognition—including 12 national student awards since 2020 and , most recently, a 2026 Honor Award in Urban Design for the Tlatelolco, Mexico City study on environmental and cultural resilience. Housed within a STEM -designated, LAAB -accredited MLA program, LAEP integrates design, ecology, and environmental planning from a global, cross-contextual, and cross cultural perspective, addressing environmental stewardship amid rapid urbanization. Faculty study and design landscapes across both international and regional territories, leading international workshops on urban design, habitat protection, and coastal resilience, and advancing this work through distinctive labs: The Just Lab, connecting landscape practice with African and Indigenous communities and the ancestral ties linking North Carolina to the African continent; the Natural Learning Initiative, creating nature-based environments to support healthy child development and community well-being in diverse and disadvantaged communities; and the Coastal Dynamics Design Lab, addressing coastal resilience through applied design along the North Carolina coast. The Natural Learning Initiative The Natural Learning Initiative ( NLI , founded in January 2000) is an interdisciplinary, cross-sector research, education, design programming, and communications lab at the College of Design, NC State University. NLI aims to create state-of-the-art environments that support healthy human development and a healthy biosphere by engaging children and families with nature in the spaces of daily life, particularly in disadvantaged, diverse communities. To achieve this goal, NLI tracks trends, research findings, and emerging approaches and disseminates information to guide innovative, nature-based design solutions, combined with education programs and public events such as design institutes, conferences, and distance education courses. The NLI team designs and implements original research studies and post-occupancy evaluations, producing findings that inform guidelines, toolkits, publications, and media disseminated via NLI’s website, YouTube channel, and downloadable resources. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The successful candidate, a full-time tenure-track/tenured Associate Professor in a 9-month faculty appointment, will dedicate 50% of their efforts to the LAEP department, including teaching courses and contributing to departmental committees. The other 50% will be allocated to NLI , focusing on developing a robust research agenda, advising doctoral students, continuing certificate programs, building partnerships and collaborations, managing NLI staff, and securing external funding. LAEP Associate Professor Duties (50% Effort) Teaching (30%): Teach on studio and one seminar/lecture course per academic year. The candidate should be able to teach design studios across scales in the MLA curriculum and address LAAB accreditation professional criteria. Courses taught may include research methods, landscape architecture history, urban theory, digital media, grading, or construction technology. Service and Governance, including curriculum advising (20%): Contribute to standard departmental committees, participate in accreditation ( LAAB ), advise LAEP students, and act as a full member of the LAEP Department Voting Faculty ( DVF ). Evaluation & Reporting: To reflect 50/50 nature of this joint appointment, the candidate will hold equal reporting lines to both units. The LAEP Department Head will evaluate teaching and departmental service, while the Associate Dean of Research will oversee NLI responsibilities. NLI Duties (under the Associate Professor role) (50% Effort) Research & Grants: Act as PI/Co-PI to identify and secure competitive extramural funding through grants, contracts, and sponsorships. Mentorship & Partnerships: Advise doctoral students whose research aligns with NLI focus areas, while also building and sustaining external partnerships, including Centers for Disease Control ( CDC ) Technical Assistance (TA) States. Duties as NLI Associate Director (Administrative Supplement) Program & Staff Management: Oversee and continue expanding NLI certificate programs, and manage dedicated NLI staff to ensure smooth daily operations. Supervisory duties : Direct supervision and management of dedicated NLI staff to ensure smooth daily operations, as well as supervision of NLI student assistants. Other Responsibilities Maintain recruitment, training, mentoring, and retention of student assistance from LAEP , other design disciplines, and elsewhere on campus. Fulfill Reappointment, Promotion, and Tenure ( RPT ) expectations, which will be equitably weighted in the Statement of Faculty Responsibilities ( SFR ). Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience A professional degree in Landscape Architecture of a closely related design discipline. Demonstrated experience teaching design studios across scales and courses that support LAAB accreditation professional criteria (e.g., research methods, landscape history, urban theory, grading). Demonstrated success in teaching and mentoring students at the graduate level. Hold a doctoral degree in a field related to NLI focus areas, preferably environment and behavior. A focus on environmental and behavior with knowledge of children and family environments. A proven record of obtaining competitive extramural funding. Evidence of academic impact, including an established record of peer-reviewed publications. Prior academic leadership and administrative experience. Other Required Qualifications Ability to teach in a studio setting Ability to apply current NLI research tools and measures. Ability to facilitate interdisciplinary collaboration. Demonstrated success in managing projects and/or multidisciplinary teams. Preferred Qualifications Hold a Master of Landscape Architecture ( MLA ) degree. Experience as an instructor, practitioner, and researcher. Prior academic leadership and administrative experience, including the duration of that experience. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 10/21/2026 Anticipated Close Date 11/18/2026; if posting is still active we are accepting and reviewing applications. Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants are required to submit: Letter of Intent ( LOI ) describing qualifications and interests, may be submitted under “Cover Letter.” CV (Curriculum Vitae) Digital portfolio or portfolio link via online application. *Note: digital portfolios and research publications may be submitted as “Other Documents.” List of references and their contact information Do not submit these materials via email. Email inquiries and nominations to the search committee co-chair, Dr. Nilda Cosco, at ngcosco@ncsu.edu Position Details Position Number 00112392 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 120401 - Landscape Architecture EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Other Document (1) Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236544": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Molecular Materials and Machines",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant Professor - Molecular Materials and Machines Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant Professor - Molecular Materials and Machines Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants should upload the following documents as part of their application: Curriculum Vitae (including a full list of publications) Cover Letter Contact Information for References Research Statement (maximum six pages) comprising a detailed plan for a research program. Teaching Statement (2 pages) highlighting pedagogical approaches, student engagement, and mentoring. An optional one-page executive summary outlining the need for any specialized equipment or infrastructure that your research program will need to be successful at NC State may be uploaded as Other Document (1) . Applications must be submitted electronically via the NCSU employment portal. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194978EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant Professor - Molecular Materials and Machines Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with experience. Work Schedule Varies based on teaching/research schedule. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Department of Chemistry About the Department The Department of Chemistry at NC State University provides professional education for chemists at the undergraduate and graduate levels; teaches introductory chemistry courses, which are needed by students enrolled in other department programs; advances the discipline of chemistry by conducting research; serves the public by sharing information about chemistry through a variety of mechanisms and services; and commits to creating environments that are in alignment with our mission, vision and values. Our department is home to award-winning faculty and is one of NC State’s top producers of patent and invention disclosures. More information about the department can be found at https://chemistry.sciences.ncsu.edu/ . While working in this department, you will be expected to foster a supportive and welcoming environment. NC State promotes an integrated approach to problem solving that transforms lives and provides leadership for social, economic, and technological development across North Carolina and around the world. NC State’s land grant mission of teaching, research and service is dedicated to the service of North Carolina and its people. Applicants are encouraged to review the institution’s mission, vision and strategic plan, and consider how their background, interest and experience would enable them to support the university. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Chemistry at North Carolina State University invites applications for a 9-month tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor in the broadly-defined areas of Molecular Materials and Machines. We seek candidates researching the design principles by which (macro)molecules, supramolecular assemblies, and designed biomolecules become functional matter. Examples include, but are not limited to: molecular machines, switches, and mechanically interlocked architectures; de novo design of biomacromolecular materials and assemblies; framework, supramolecular, and discrete molecular materials with transport, switching, or device function; and adaptive, dynamic, and stimuli-responsive molecular matter. Experimental programs as well as those that integrate computation and theory will be considered. Programs that integrate or aim to build toward data-driven/AI-guided design and/or autonomous/closed-loop experimentation are particularly encouraged. In this role, you will have access to extensive shared facilities, including the METRIC center for mass spectrometry, NMR / EPR , and X-ray crystallography; time-resolved spectroscopy ( Imaging and Kinetics Spectroscopy Lab ); bioanalytical instrumentation ( BioCore ); electron microscopy ( Analytical Instrumentation Facility ); nanofabrication ( NNF ); device characterization through the ORaCEL organic-electronics labs; campus high-performance computing ; and the self-driving laboratories of the NC State-led $20M NSF SPEED autonomous-experimentation facility with expected availability in 2027. Key Responsibilities: Develop a robust, externally funded research program. Lead an independent research program and engage in collaborative research at North Carolina State University and the Research Triangle. Teach organic- and physical-chemistry and related topics at the graduate and undergraduate level. Mentor graduate students and other scholars. Other Responsibilities Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience A PhD in Chemistry or a closely related field from an appropriately accredited institution is required by the start date. Other Required Qualifications N/A Preferred Qualifications Demonstrable ability to carry out innovative and impactful research. Demonstrable expertise in the design of (bio)molecular materials and machines, or related topics. Demonstrable interest in teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Demonstrable interest in mentoring and training graduate students. At least one year of post-doctoral experience. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 10/21/2026 Anticipated Close Date 11/29/2026 [If the posting is still active after this date, applications are still being accepted and will be reviewed.] Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants should upload the following documents as part of their application: Curriculum Vitae (including a full list of publications) Cover Letter Contact Information for References Research Statement (maximum six pages) comprising a detailed plan for a research program. Teaching Statement (2 pages) highlighting pedagogical approaches, student engagement, and mentoring. An optional one-page executive summary outlining the need for any specialized equipment or infrastructure that your research program will need to be successful at NC State may be uploaded as Other Document (1) . Applications must be submitted electronically via the NCSU employment portal. Position Details Position Number 00112399 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 170701 - Chemistry EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for References Research Statement Teaching Statement Optional Documents Other Document (1) NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
