    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236493": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Genetics",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant Teaching Professor - Genetics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant Teaching Professor - Genetics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Cover letter (1 page) Resume/Curriculum Vitae Statement of teaching philosophy (1-2 pages) Evidence of teaching excellence, which may include class evaluations, outcomes of education research or assessment, syllabi, lecture slides, class activities, or other documentation (10 page maximum) (Other Document 2) Contact information for references Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194984EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant Teaching Professor - Genetics Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with education and experience ($75,000-$80,000) Work Schedule Core Business hours: Monday - Friday; 8:00 AM - 5:00 PM; hours will vary based on teaching and laboratory schedule, this is a 40 hour week minimum commitment. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Biological Sciences About the Department The Department of Biological Sciences, within the College of Sciences at NC State University, is dedicated to research and teaching in a broad range of aspects of the biological sciences. The Department has strong undergraduate, graduate, and postdoctoral programs and substantial extramural support to develop and maintain integrative research programs. Additionally, the Department partners with other life sciences units across the University to enhance its mission to conduct interdisciplinary research and training programs. While working in this department, you will be expected to foster a supportive and welcoming environment. NC State promotes an integrated approach to problem solving that transforms lives and provides leadership for social, economic, and technological development across North Carolina and around the world. NC State’s land grant mission of teaching, research and service is dedicated to the service of North Carolina and its people. Applicants are encouraged to review the institution’s mission, vision and strategic plan, and consider how their background, interest and experience would enable them to support the university. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Biological Sciences at NC State University invites applications for an Assistant Teaching Professor in Genetics, beginning in August 2027. This 9-month, professional track appointment carries an 80% teaching effort and 20% service effort. This position supports the undergraduate Genetics Program through teaching, advising, and opportunities to contribute to curriculum development and undergraduate-focused research. As an Assistant Teaching Professor, you will help students build a strong foundation in genetics by connecting core concepts in population and molecular genetics with their applications across the life sciences. Through your thoughtful, evidence-informed instruction, students will develop critical thinking skills, apply scientific principles, and prepare for further study and careers in the life sciences. Key Responsibilities Teach undergraduate genetics courses, including “Principles of Genetics”, “Population, Quantitative, and Evolutionary Genetics”, and/or “Molecular Genetics”, using effective, evidence-informed approaches. Courses taught may vary by semester, with an estimated teaching load of 6–9 credit hours per semester. Develop or enhance courses that reflect your disciplinary strengths and support the evolving needs of the undergraduate curriculum, including opportunities in bioinformatics or computational biology. Advise undergraduate students and support their academic progress through the Genetics Program. Coordinate laboratory courses on a rotating basis, as needed, and mentor and supervise graduate teaching assistants. Contribute to departmental service, serve on graduate student committees, and participate in other academic activities aligned with departmental needs and your interests. Pursue opportunities in undergraduate-focused research and discipline-based education research. If you enjoy helping students connect complex genetic concepts to real-world questions, value thoughtful teaching, and bring a collaborative approach to working with students and colleagues, we invite you to apply and join the Department of Biological Sciences at NC State University. Other Responsibilities In addition to the core responsibilities of this role, there may be occasional opportunities to take on additional duties. This offers an opportunity to build on your skills, explore new areas, and gain a deeper understanding of the department’s operations. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience PhD in Genetics or another life science field; or relevant degree. Other Required Qualifications Expertise in population genetics and molecular genetics, demonstrated through academic training, research, or other relevant disciplinary experience. Demonstrated teaching experience through previous teaching assistant experience or teaching undergraduate-level courses in genetics or other biological sciences. Preferred Qualifications n/a Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 10/21/2026 Anticipated Close Date 12/2/2026; if posting is active, we are still accepting and reviewing applications. Special Instructions to Applicants Cover letter (1 page) Resume/Curriculum Vitae Statement of teaching philosophy (1-2 pages) Evidence of teaching excellence, which may include class evaluations, outcomes of education research or assessment, syllabi, lecture slides, class activities, or other documentation (10 page maximum) (Other Document 2) Contact information for references Position Details Position Number 00112401 Position Type Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 172201 - Biological Sciences EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Other Document (1) Other Document (2) Contact Information for References Resume/CV Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236473": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Elementary Teacher Education",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant Professor in Elementary Teacher Education Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant Professor in Elementary Teacher Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include the following as a part of your application packet: 1. Cover Letter 2. CV 3. Teaching Statement 4. Contact information for References Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194860EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant Professor in Elementary Teacher Education Anticipated Hiring Range $80,000 - $84,000 Work Schedule 40 hours a week Job Location Raleigh NC Department TELS About the Department About the NC State College of Education As one of the nation’s top-ranked colleges of education, NC State’s College of Education leads the way in North Carolina in preparing extraordinary educators, conducting transformational research, and engaging communities where they are to improve the educational outcomes of all learners and advance the greater good. The college’s faculty are widely-recognized thought leaders who use their research to transform the practice of teaching, learning, and leading. They have particular strengths in improving technology-enhanced learning and teaching; fostering community-based learning and PK-16 partnerships; and innovating leadership and workforce development, educational policy, and evaluation. About two-thirds of the faculty are grant active. They are engaged in over 225 active projects totaling $151 million, making them the most productive in terms of research activity compared with other colleges of education in North Carolina and among the Top 5% in the nation. In FY24, the college’s research expenditures exceeded $20 million. The college has over 1,600 students studying across five graduate certificates, seven undergraduate majors, two undergraduate minors, 13 master’s degrees, three Ph.D., and two Ed.D. programs housed in three academic departments: Educational Leadership, Policy, and Human Development; Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics Education; and Teacher Education and Learning Sciences, with approximately 130 tenure-track and professional-track faculty, 110 support and professional staff, and about 160 graduate and teaching assistants. The College of Education is also home to the Belk Center for Community College Leadership and Research, the Friday Institute for Educational Innovation, and Elevate, NC State’s inclusive postsecondary education program for students with intellectual and developmental disabilities. The college has over 18,000 living alumni, with over 6,000 working in public schools in every county in North Carolina. Those who are teachers rate among the highest in effectiveness on surveys of school employers in North Carolina. NC State promotes an integrated approach to problem solving that transforms lives and provides leadership for social, economic, and technological development across North Carolina and around the world. NC State’s land grant mission of teaching, research and service is dedicated to the service of North Carolina and its people. Applicants are encouraged to review the institution’s mission, vision and strategic plan, and consider how their background, interest and experience would enable them to support the university. The Department of Teacher Education and Learning Sciences ( TELS ) comprises over 40 full-time faculty members preparing more than 500 undergraduate and graduate students and 200 students in alternative teacher licensure programs. We prepare students to work in a range of fields across various programs that include Elementary Education (with a STEM focus), Educational Psychology, Educational Equity, Literacy and English Language Arts, Learning Design and Technology, Middle and Secondary English Language Arts, Social Studies, Multilingual Education, and Special Education. We advance education through scholarship, leadership, and advocacy. We prepare professionals who are committed to provide learning opportunities for all and who have deep content knowledge, demonstrate strong working knowledge of effective pedagogies, and realize the potential of digital technologies to enhance learning. We shape the field of education by engaging in research that addresses current challenges, and by participating in cross-disciplinary work that deals with real problems in forward-looking ways. The department exemplifies an innovative merging of teacher education and the learning sciences that results in new pathways for teaching, scholarship, leadership, and service. The preparation that our students receive is unmatched in scope, priorities, and outcomes, assuring that our graduates are able to make profound contributions to education and society. In addition to the degree earning programs above, TELS also offers an inclusive postsecondary education program, Elevate. Elevate is a university-wide initiative designed for North Carolina residents with intellectual and developmental disabilities ( IDD ) and offers educational credentials, such as certificates. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Teacher Education and Learning Sciences ( TELS ) invites applications for an Assistant Professor in Elementary Teacher Education to be affiliated with undergraduate and graduate studies in elementary teaching and learning. This is a tenure-track appointment at the Assistant Professor level, with teaching, scholarship, service, and outreach expectations. We are seeking those who are scholars in elementary teacher education who will lead and contribute to research on approaches and programs that prepare pre-service teachers. You will engage in research primarily focused on elementary teacher preparation programs’ features and impact. This might include elements such as modality (e.g., face-to-face, hybrid, online), structure (e.g., traditional four-year programs, part-time programs for practicing teachers, competency-based education), or pathway (e.g., bachelor’s degree, master’s degree, residency, registered apprenticeship). Additionally, you will submit proposals for internal/external funding in support of the related research. The ideal candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in elementary teacher preparation, including the Master of Arts in Teaching ( MAT ) program, with a strong preference for those who teach elementary social studies education. As a faculty member, you will provide service and leadership to the Elementary Education program area, the department, college, and university. You will participate in outreach and engagement activities with elementary schools locally and across North Carolina, and collaborate with faculty within the department, college, and across the university. Position Responsibilities Maintain a high level of scholarly research, publication, and grant-writing activity that aligns with a tenure track position in a university with high research activity. Produce high quality research on pre-service teacher preparation programs, features, and impact. Seek external funding for research and development activities. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in elementary education, with a strong preference for social studies pre-service teacher education graduate and undergraduate programs Recruit, advise, and mentor graduate students and serve on doctoral committees. Engage in collaborative research with other faculty and researchers within the College of Education, including the Friday Institute for Educational Innovation and the Belk Center for Community College leadership, as well as across the university. Provide service and leadership in the elementary education program, department, college, university, and professional organizations. Participate in outreach and engagement for department and college initiatives with underserved communities and high need areas and engaging with stakeholders across the state of North Carolina. If you are passionate about preparing future elementary educators and interested in teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in elementary teacher preparation, including the Master of Arts in Teaching ( MAT ) program, with expertise in elementary social studies education, we encourage you to apply and join our faculty. Other Responsibilities N/A Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Doctorate in Teacher Education, Curriculum & Instruction, Elementary Education, or a related field Other Required Qualifications Experience teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses in elementary education Experience in pre-service teacher preparation K-6 teaching experience Scholarship and funding record commensurate with experience Demonstrated potential for excellence in research, teaching, extension, and service Demonstrated ability to work effectively with students and individuals from a wide range of backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences Demonstrated ability to support students with varied academic and professional needs Preferred Qualifications At least 3 years of K-6 teaching experience A record of publication and presentation commensurate with experience, with preference to work related to the scholarship of teaching and learning Experience facilitating teacher professional development Success in building relationships with schools and districts Required License(s) or Certification(s) N.A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/03/2026 Anticipated Close Date 11/02/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Please include the following as a part of your application packet: 1. Cover Letter 2. CV 3. Teaching Statement 4. Contact information for References Position Details Position Number 00112293 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 131101 - Teacher Education and Learning Sciences (TELS) EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Teaching Statement Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236450": {
      "title": "Small Animal Internal Medicine Residency - Clinician Investigator",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Small Animal Internal Medicine Residency - Clinician Investigator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Small Animal Internal Medicine Residency - Clinician Investigator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191790PD Position Number 00108720 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 195001 - Department of Clinical Sciences Department 195001 - Department of Clinical Sciences Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties The Internal Medicine Clinician Investigator Program provides clinical training in small animal internal medicine and graduate research training toward the PhD degree. The residency portion of the program meets or exceeds the training requirements established by the ACVIM for candidates seeking board certification in Small Animal Internal Medicine. The primary objectives of the program are to develop clinical expertise in veterinary internal medicine, gain experience in didactic and clinical teaching, and become proficient in basic and applied research. The duration of the program varies according to each student’s ability to satisfy program requirements, but will be no less than five years, with the residency component of the program comprising the first three years. The Clinician Investigator Program is structured and rigorous, requires a team-oriented approach, and embodies a spirit of cooperation amongst clinical and basic science faculty. The program was designed to satisfy the needs of those individuals who are seeking a career in academic veterinary medicine, industry, or government. Successful completion of the program is dependent upon attracting candidates of the highest caliber who are capable of excelling in this demanding program. Because of the breadth and complexity of the program, the clinician investigator will participate in a varied group of activities with increasing levels of responsibility. Clinical activity is most intensive in the first year of the program and clinical training is as for an Internal Medicine Residency Program. During the second and third years, both clinical and research responsibilities are scheduled. The remaining years of the program are devoted primarily to research activities. Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include the supervision and education of veterinary students, interns, and other residents; patient care and client communication; and progressively increasing autonomy in diagnostic and therapeutic patient management. Attendance and participation in daily case rounds, intern/resident rounds, journal club, advanced medicine rounds, and the House Officer Seminar Program are required. Clinician investigators must maintain a case log and endoscopy log to allow the CI and residency committee to determine if seeing an appropriate balance of case material. Clinician investigators are expected to gain acceptance into graduate school by January 15th deadline (by year 1 of program), and complete 2-3 laboratory rotations (during years one and two) and identify a graduate mentor by the end of year two. For specific information on the clinician investigator program, please visit: https://cvm.ncsu.edu/education/residencies/small-animal-internal-medicine/ For specific information on the residency component of the program, please visit: https://www.acvim.org/ Starting in the second year, clinician investigators are paid bi-weekly instead of monthly. In the fall and spring semesters there is exemption from some taxes but student fees may be owed (approximately 1,300.00/semester, see https://studentservices.ncsu.edu/your-money/tuition-and-fees/graduate-students/ for additional information). There is no exemption from any taxes during the summer semesters. Other Work/Responsibilities Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule 7am - 7pm, may vary depending on weekends and holidays Department Required Skills One-year rotating internship or equivalent experience is required by the department. Applicants must be committed to completing combined small animal internal residency and PhD program. The primary objectives of the Clinician Investigators are to obtain board certification by the American College of Veterinary Internal Medicine (Small Animal), gain experience in clinical and didactic teaching, and proficiency in basic and applied research through the completion of a PhD program. Must be able to lift up to 50 pounds. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Applicants seeking a career in academic veterinary medicine, industry, or government. Must have DVM or equivalent degree, and one year rotating internship or equivalent broad-based post- DVM clinical experience. For applicants with a degree from a school outside of the U.S., please review this website for information on degree certification: https://www.wes.org/. Final candidates are required to have their degree equivalency verified. A list of the fees associated with this process can be found here: https://www.wes.org/evaluations-and-fees/. Required License or Certification Eligible for North Carolina Veterinary Licensure and/or faculty certificate under the supervision of the NCSU College of Veterinary Medicine, Veterinary Health Complex. Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $54,000 If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 10/15/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236306 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have (or will you have by date of hire) a DVM or equivalent degree? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents Transcripts NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236444": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Scholar",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191777PD Position Number 00112341 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 140201 - Chemical & Biomolecular Engineering Department 140201 - Chemical & Biomolecular Engineering Job City & State Raleigh, North Carolina Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties The Postdoctoral Research Scholar will lead the experimental research program on liquid electrolytes for wide-temperature lithium-ion batteries. The objective is a single liquid electrolyte that supports reliable Li-ion full-cell operation across a wide temperature range, where conventional carbonate electrolytes freeze in the cold and degrade at elevated temperatures. The Postdoctoral Research Scholar will design and formulate multi-component electrolytes (salt selection, binary and ternary solvent blending, fluorinated diluents, and additive engineering); build and test coin and pouch full cells under standardized protocols in environmental chambers spanning the full temperature window; characterize Li+ solvation structure and electrode/electrolyte interphases; carry out flammability and thermal-safety screening; and deconvolute electrolyte from electrode contributions to cell performance. The Postdoctoral Research Scholar will also be responsible for day-to-day execution of the NC State scope of work, for supervising the graduate and undergraduate students assigned to the project, and for preparing the deliverables, data packages, and technical reports owed to the prime contractor. Duties and Responsibilities include: Design, formulate, and optimize liquid electrolytes for wide-temperature lithium-ion cells, including salt selection, binary/ternary solvent blending, fluorinated diluents, and additive engineering. Assemble and test coin and pouch full cells ( NMC ||graphite and related chemistries) in an argon glovebox, including electrode slurry preparation, coating, calendering, and cell crimping. Execute standardized electrochemical evaluation across the full target temperature range using environmental and cryogenic chambers: galvanostatic cycling, rate capability, impedance spectroscopy, cyclic voltammetry, and three-electrode/reference measurements. Characterize electrolyte physicochemical properties and Li+ solvation structure (ionic conductivity, viscosity, freezing and phase behavior, Raman, FTIR , NMR ) and electrode-electrolyte interphases ( XPS , SEM / EDS , and related tools). Perform flammability and thermal-safety screening of candidate formulations under approved safety protocols. Analyze, curate, and archive experimental data; maintain complete and auditable electronic laboratory records. Prepare monthly and quarterly technical progress reports, milestone data packages, and deliverables for the prime contractor and the Army technical point of contact; participate in sponsor teleconferences and program reviews. Write and submit peer-reviewed manuscripts and conference abstracts and present results at national meetings. Train, supervise, and mentor graduate and undergraduate students working on the project. Maintain and troubleshoot laboratory instrumentation (gloveboxes, battery cyclers, environmental chambers, potentiostats. and coordinate calibration and service. Comply with all EHS requirements for handling flammable organic solvents, lithium salts, lithium metal, compressed gases, dry ice and cryogens, and for battery testing. Other Work/Responsibilities Assist with laboratory management: chemical inventory, hazardous waste streams, ordering of supplies, and onboarding of new group members. Serve as a laboratory safety contact for the battery testing space and help maintain standard operating procedures. Contribute preliminary data and text to future proposals to DoD, DOE , NSF , and industry. Support intellectual-property activities, including invention disclosures arising from the project. Assist with outreach, laboratory tours, and hosting of sponsor and collaborator visits. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday-Friday 8am-5pm Department Required Skills Electrolyte preparation and handling of moisture- and air-sensitive materials (glovebox, Schlenk/air-free technique). Lithium-ion cell fabrication: electrode slurry casting, calendering, cell assembly and crimping. Electrochemical testing and interpretation: galvanostatic cycling, rate capability, electrochemical impedance spectroscopy, cyclic voltammetry; operation of battery cyclers and potentiostats. Quantitative data analysis and scientific plotting (Python, MATLAB , Origin, or equivalent). Scientific writing and presentation; ability to draft manuscripts and sponsor progress reports independently. Ability to work safely and independently with flammable organic solvents and lithium-containing materials, and to work effectively with students and external sponsors. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education 2+ years of research experience in liquid electrolyte design for lithium-ion or lithium-metal batteries beyond the doctoral degree. Experience with low-temperature and/or high-temperature battery testing and with environmental, cryogenic, or thermal chambers. Experience probing Li+ solvation structure (Raman, FTIR , NMR ) and interphase chemistry ( XPS , SEM / EDS , cryo-EM, TOF - SIMS ). Experience with multi-layer pouch cell fabrication and scale-up. Experience with flammability, thermal-runaway, or other battery safety testing. Prior experience on projects, including milestone-driven reporting. Experience mentoring graduate or undergraduate researchers. Required License or Certification N/A Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $61,000 If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many 2 Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 09/17/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/235119 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other (Open Ended Question) If you learned about this vacancy from \"other\" or were asked for additional information in question #1, please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
