    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236666": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Agricultural Economics - Research &amp; Teaching",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant Professor in Agricultural Economics - Research &amp; Teaching Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant Professor in Agricultural Economics - Research & Teaching Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. As part of your application please attach the following: 1. Cover Letter 2. CV 3. Job Market Paper/Other Research Paper (other document 1) 4. Contact Information for Professional References To ensure full consideration, we encourage all applicants to submit their materials by November 23, 2026. If you have specific questions about the position, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Roderick \"Rod\" M. Rejesus ( rmrejesu@ncsu.edu ). Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194986EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant Professor in Agricultural Economics - Research & Teaching Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with education and experience Work Schedule Core Business Hours: Monday - Friday; 8:00 AM - 5:00 PM; flexibility and variable schedule will be determined based on teaching and research needs. This position requires 40 hours a week minimum commitment. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Agriculture & Resource Economics About the Department The Department of Agricultural and Resource Economics ( ARE ) embodies excellence in research, teaching, and extension in the economics of agriculture and the economics of natural resources and the environment. Dedicated, student-focused faculty teach diverse courses and nurture industry connections to help students pursue rewarding careers. Researchers engage students in relevant, applied research. Extension specialists and associates conduct research-based education and training activities that benefit local and global communities including North Carolina’s vibrant agricultural sector (9th ranked nationally in cash receipts from farming in 2022 ( USDA NASS )). ARE offers undergraduate major and minor programs in agricultural business management and a concentration in biological sciences business management within the agricultural business management program. At the graduate level, the department via the Economics Graduate Program, offers a Master of Science degree and a Master of Economics degree, and a Ph.D. degree in economics. The department is also set to launch the Master in Agribusiness Management ( MABM ) degree program, which blends agricultural sciences with business principles—analytics, sales, marketing, entrepreneurship and policy. These instructional programs are enriched by faculty members with extension and research activities which contribute to the relevance and thoroughness of the teaching program. ARE is part of the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences, which conducts outstanding research, teaching, and extension programs and plays a vital role in North Carolina agriculture, food and fiber systems, environmental quality enhancement, and economic development. ARE is housed in Nelson Hall along with The Poole College of Management ( PCOM ) on the NCSU Campus in Raleigh, North Carolina. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Agricultural and Resource Economics ( ARE ) in the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences ( CALS ) at North Carolina State University invites qualified applicants for a tenure-track Assistant Professor faculty position in agricultural economics. This position will be split 50% Research and 50% Teaching. This is a 9-month / academic year based appointment. In this role, you will contribute to the department’s academic mission through a balanced program of teaching, research, and service in agricultural economics. You will engage with students and colleagues across the department and university while advancing scholarship in agricultural economics and supporting the development of future researchers. Responsibilities: Teach two courses annually at the undergraduate or graduate level, based on departmental needs, including PhD-level field courses in agricultural economics, and supervise PhD students. Establish and maintain a research program in agricultural economics that is effectively supported by extramural funding and produces publications in high-quality peer-reviewed journals. Contribute service to the profession, department, college, and university while developing a research program that complements existing expertise in Agricultural and Resource Economics and, where appropriate, connects with faculty in other departments. We invite you to bring your scholarly interests, teaching, and experience to a department committed to advancing agricultural and resource economics. Through your work with students and colleagues, you will help shape the next generation of researchers and contribute to the department’s academic community. Other Responsibilities In addition to the core responsibilities of this role, there may be occasional opportunities to take on additional duties. This offers an opportunity to build on your skills, explore new areas, and gain a deeper understanding of the department’s operations. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Ph.D. degree in agricultural economics, economics, or a closely related discipline. Other Required Qualifications Evidence of the ability to develop and sustain a research program aligned with the land-grant mission, with potential to produce peer-reviewed publications in reputable agricultural economics, economics, or related field journals and to pursue extramural funding. Expertise in one or more areas in the consumer or demand side of agricultural and applied economics, such as consumer demand analysis, agricultural marketing, commodity markets, futures trading, price analysis, food economics, industrial organization, or behavioral economics, with the ability to develop an innovative research agenda and contribute to teaching in relevant areas. Research interests and expertise that complement the Department of Agricultural and Resource Economics’ existing strengths and offer opportunities for collaboration across research, teaching, and outreach. Preferred Qualifications Prior teaching experience at the undergraduate and graduate level Evidence and experience applying cutting-edge econometric, behavioral or experimental methods to research areas in the consumer and demand side of agricultural economics, including (but not limited to) the following topics: food demand, consumer behavior, human nutrition and health, food safety, food supply chains and risk, retailing strategy, new product development, labeling, demand systems, price transmission, futures and options markets, market structure and power in agriculture, contracting relationships, food waste, and food policy/regulations. Required License(s) or Certification(s) Valid NC driver’s license or the ability to obtain within 60 days of start. Valid NC Driver's License required Yes Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 10/26/2026 Anticipated Close Date 03/01/2027; if posting is still active, we are accepting and reviewing applications. Special Instructions to Applicants As part of your application please attach the following: 1. Cover Letter 2. CV 3. Job Market Paper/Other Research Paper (other document 1) 4. Contact Information for Professional References To ensure full consideration, we encourage all applicants to submit their materials by November 23, 2026. If you have specific questions about the position, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Roderick “Rod” M. Rejesus ( rmrejesu@ncsu.edu ). Position Details Position Number 00000285 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.00 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 118001 - Agriculture & Resource Economics EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have, or will you have by date of hire, a PhD degree in Agricultural Economics, Economics, or a closely related discipline? Yes No * Do you have a valid NC Driver's license or the ability to obtain one within 60 days of your start date? Yes No Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Other Document (1) Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236658": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Electrical &amp; Computer Engineering",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant Professor - Electrical &amp; Computer Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant Professor - Electrical & Computer Engineering Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications will be reviewed as they are received. Applicants will receive consideration starting November 1, 2026. In addition to a fully completed application, applicants should submit the following online: cover letter, curriculum vitae, research statement, teaching statement, and names and complete contact information for four references, including email address and phone numbers. Candidates can obtain information about the department and its research programs, as well as more detail about the positions advertised at http://www.ece.ncsu.edu. Inquiries may be sent via email to the Faculty Search Committee Chair, at ecefacultyhire@ncsu.edu Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194993EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant Professor - Electrical & Computer Engineering Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with education/experience Work Schedule Academic Position - Hours Vary Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Electrical and Computer Engineering About the Department The Electrical and Computer Engineering ( ECE ) Department is one of the top 10 suppliers of ECE talent at the BS level in the US, and ranks in the top ECE Departments in total annual research expenditures ( ASEE ). The department is located in state-of-the-art facilities on NC State’s Centennial Campus. Its undergraduate EE and CpE degree programs have been ranked in the Top 20 and Top 30, respectively, by US news and World Report. The University is located in the technology-rich Research Triangle metropolitan area, and ECE faculty members collaborate routinely with local industry. The Research Triangle area is frequently recognized in nationwide surveys as one of the best places to live in the U.S. We enjoy outstanding public schools, affordable housing, and great weather, all in the proximity of the mountains and the seashore. Candidates can obtain information about the department and its research programs, as well as more details about the positions advertised at http://www.ece.ncsu.edu . NC State promotes an integrated approach to problem solving that transforms lives and provides leadership for social, economic, and technological development across North Carolina and around the world. NC State’s land grant mission of teaching, research, and service is dedicated to the service of North Carolina and its people. Applicants are encouraged to review the institution’s mission, vision, and strategic plan, and consider how their background, interest, and experience would enable them to support the university. Discover the possibilities at NC State University and the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering for your professional and personal growth. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering is seeking to fill multiple tenure-track faculty positions at the rank of Assistant Professor beginning in August 2027 as part of NC State’s strategic engineering expansion. The department is seeking excellent candidates in the following areas Outstanding candidates outside these areas will be considered based on the candidates’ qualifications and the strengths of the department . : Quantum : Quantum computing architectures, quantum sensing, quantum communications, and hardware implementations for quantum information science. Robotics : Autonomous systems, control theory, sensing and perception, drone and unmanned systems, and novel applications of robotics across domains such as machine learning, healthcare, defense applications, and environmental monitoring. Power Electronics and Motor Drives : Power semiconductor devices, drive architectures, and applications in renewable energy and electric vehicles. Power electronics for data centers are also of particular interest. Semiconductors : Advanced materials and device technologies with emphasis on wide-bandgap semiconductors. Candidates will contribute to undergraduate and graduate student education, likely teaching classes in areas as assigned. Other Responsibilities Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Ph.D. or equivalent in electrical or computer engineering or a related discipline at the time of appointment. Other Required Qualifications Strong commitment to academic and research excellence, and an outstanding research record commensurate with the expectations of a major research university. Demonstrated the potential to build a strong research program and an excellent teaching record. Preferred Qualifications N/A Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 10/26/2026 Anticipated Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applications will be reviewed as they are received. Applicants will receive consideration starting November 1, 2026. In addition to a fully completed application, applicants should submit the following online: cover letter, curriculum vitae, research statement, teaching statement, and names and complete contact information for four references, including email address and phone numbers. Candidates can obtain information about the department and its research programs, as well as more detail about the positions advertised at http://www.ece.ncsu.edu. Inquiries may be sent via email to the Faculty Search Committee Chair, at ecefacultyhire@ncsu.edu Position Details Position Number 00102131 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.00 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 140401 - Electrical & Computer Engineering EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other * If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Which of the following describes your primary area of research? Quantum Robotics Power Electronics and Motor Drives Semiconductors Other (please describe in Question #5) * Which of the following describes your secondary area of research? Quantum Robotics Power Electronics and Motor Drives Semiconductors Other (please describe in Question #5) If you selected \"Other\" for either questions #3 or #4, please include your primary and secondary research area here: (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for References Research Statement Teaching Statement Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
