    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236654": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant/Associate Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant/Associate Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194970EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor Anticipated Hiring Range Salary commensurate upon experience and qualifications Work Schedule varies as needed Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Lampe Joint Department of BME About the Department Founded in 2003, the Lampe UNC /NC State Joint Department of Biomedical Engineering is a unique collaboration between North Carolina’s two flagship universities: The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill ( UNC -CH) and North Carolina State University (NC State). The Joint Department is a unique partnership that unites two universities with shared graduate and undergraduate programs in a single administrative department with a single chairperson. The nationally ranked UNC Hospitals and School of Medicine at UNC -CH provide an excellent clinical environment for interactions and translation, College of Arts and Sciences forms the academic core of the Carolina experience. College of Engineering at NC State, ranked one of the finest engineering and computer science schools in the world, offers state-of-the-art facilities for students and faculty engaged in vital areas of research and technology transfer. The Lampe Joint Department is on track to realize its ambitious vision of becoming a leader in real-world results and its mission to unite engineering and medicine to improve lives. The Joint Department has grown to encompass 54 primary teaching and research faculty members (including five endowed chairs) and over 600 undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral students. With more than $25 million in research expenditures, BME students benefit from the robust research portfolios, the exceptional education, and the vast resources of these world-class public universities. Among biomedical engineering departments, the Joint Department is ranked in the top 15 globally and top 10 domestically (Shanghai Rankings) and in the top 5 by total BME BS Graduates ( ASEE ). Established in 2010 by Dr. Ross W. Lampe Jr., the endowed Lampe Distinguished Professorship in BME supports the recruitment and retention of internationally recognized faculty to the Joint Department. Learn more about the Joint Department at https://www.bme.unc.edu/ . Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Lampe Joint Department of Biomedical Engineering is a supportive, highly collaborative community driven by a shared mission: to improve human quality of life through rigorous study, analysis, research, and the design and translation of innovative technologies that benefit the people of North Carolina and the broader global community. In this role, candidates will join a vibrant department that values interdisciplinary thinking and real-world impact. We seek outstanding faculty candidates conducting research in areas that complement or expand our strengths in Biomedical Microdevices, Rehabilitation Engineering, Biomedical Imaging, Pharmacoengineering, and Regenerative Medicine. Lampe BME’s mission is to “Unite Engineering and Medicine to Improve Lives,” and our goal is to make an impact through ideation, translation, and commercialization of technologies to have an impact on human health and well-being. Candidates will have the opportunity to grow and sustain an independent research program while collaborating across engineering, basic sciences, and clinical disciplines. Patenting, licensing, and startup companies that license faculty’s University IP are highly encouraged. The position includes a primary appointment at NC State University with tenure home within the College of Engineering, access to shared resources at both NC State and UNC–Chapel Hill, and laboratory space located in Engineering Building 3 on NC State’s Centennial Campus—at the heart of the College of Engineering. Key Responsibilities: Establish, maintain, and grow an independent, externally funded research program in Biomedical Engineering. Engage in interdisciplinary research collaborations with engineering faculty, basic science researchers, and/or clinical investigators. Contribute to the department’s research mission through scholarship that advances biomedical technologies and improves human health. Teach and contribute to undergraduate and graduate education in biomedical engineering, in areas aligned with your expertise. Mentor undergraduate, graduate, and postdoctoral trainees and contribute to a supportive, open academic environment. Participate in service activities that support the department, college, and broader academic community. If you are a scholar looking to build an impactful biomedical engineering research program in a collaborative environment, who is motivated by translating research into technologies that improve human health, and is energized by teaching, mentoring and shaping the next generation, we encourage you to apply. This position is for a tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor in all areas related to Biomedical Engineering. Rank will be determined based on qualifications and experience. In addition to core responsibilities, there will be occasional opportunities to take on additional duties that support the department’s academic and research missions. Other Responsibilities Candidates will be expected to contribute to undergraduate and graduate student education, likely teaching classes in areas of pharmacoengineering. Successful candidates are expected to establish active externally funded research programs and to achieve excellence in teaching and training at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Qualified candidates should have a doctoral degree in Biomedical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Physics, or a related field. Appointment at the Assistant Professor rank requires evidence of scholarly productivity relative to career stage and clear potential to establish an independent, externally funded research program. Appointment at the Associate Professor rank requires a sustained record of scholarly excellence, including peer-reviewed publications, successful external funding, and leadership in interdisciplinary research. Other Required Qualifications Demonstrated commitment to advancing biomedical engineering research that improves human health and quality of life. Ability to develop and sustain an independent, externally funded research program. Strong capacity for interdisciplinary collaboration with engineering faculty, basic science researchers, and/or clinical investigators. Record of scholarly activity, including dissemination of research through peer-reviewed publications and professional presentations. Ability to contribute effectively to undergraduate and graduate education through teaching and mentoring. Excellent written and verbal communication skills to support research dissemination, collaboration, teaching, and training. Alignment with, or potential to complement, departmental research strengths in biomedical microdevices, rehabilitation engineering, biomedical imaging, pharmacoengineering, or regenerative medicine. Interest in translational research pathways, including commercialization and/or application in human clinical populations, where appropriate. Preferred Qualifications Evidence of excellence in teaching, mentoring, advising, and training students and trainees at the undergraduate, graduate, and postdoctoral levels. Academic scholarship that will integrate well with the College of Engineering Demonstrated leadership or coordination of interdisciplinary research initiatives or teams. Experience securing external research funding as a principal investigator. Research experience that demonstrates a clear pathway to translation, commercialization, clinical application, or protection of intellectual property, with a strong preference for bench-driven engineering science and collaboration across core engineering disciplines. Experience engaging with external partners, including industry or clinical collaborators Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 10/16/2026 Anticipated Close Date Open until filled Special Instructions to Applicants Position Details Position Number 00111817 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.00 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 147501 - Lampe Joint Department of BME EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you selected \"Other\" for the previous question, please provide the source you learned about this opportunity from. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Contact Information for References Research Statement Teaching Statement Brief Statement of Teaching Philosophy and Research Interests Resume/CV Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236795": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Assistant / Associate / Full Professor",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Open Rank - Assistant / Associate / Full Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Open Rank - Assistant / Associate / Full Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In addition to your application please submit: 1. Cover Letter 2. Resume/CV 3. Contact information for at least three references. 4. Research Statement 5. Teaching Statement Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194919EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Open Rank - Assistant / Associate / Full Professor Anticipated Hiring Range Rank and Salary will be commensurate with education and experience. Work Schedule Core Business Hours: Monday - Friday; 8:00 am - 5:00 pm; hours vary depending on teaching and research schedules. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Nuclear Engineering About the Department The Department of Nuclear Engineering offers undergraduate and graduate degrees in Nuclear Engineering. We are the only nuclear engineering program in the state of North Carolina and one of the premier departments in the southeast United States. The Carolinas currently contributes to the advancement of the nuclear enterprise regionally, nationally and internationally. The State of North Carolina has accepted new/updated energy policy with accelerated clean energy strategy to achieve net-zero complete transition by 2050, which include the nuclear energy as part of clean energy mix. The State of North Carolina is also committed to expanding engineering education and research including the expansion of COE at NCSU to address the growing need of advanced engineering skill in emerging areas. Nationally and internationally the United States is leading the clean energy economy of the future with initiatives across a range of sectors and all stages of innovation: research, development, and deployment. The advanced nuclear reactor technology will be an important contributor to a decarbonized power sector and net zero future. Moving to a net-zero economy would create millions of new jobs worldwide by 2030 across energy, construction, and automotive sectors, 65% of which will be high-skilled jobs. The United States is committed to realizing not only the emissions reductions potential, but also the economic growth and jobs creation opportunities across key sectors. Through collaborative efforts of various stakeholders, NC State’s Nuclear Engineering Department is increasing its footprint on the national and global level in both advanced nuclear energy developments and implementations and state-of-the-art nuclear science and engineering applications in emerging technological and digital engineering areas. With an increasing faculty population and research areas/projects, there is greater opportunity for learning in the broad areas of advanced nuclear reactor engineering, radiation detection and admeasurements, nuclear materials, security and non-proliferation, computational science and digital engineering, plasma science and engineering, radiological and waste engineering, and advanced nuclear applications in emerging high-technology, bioengineering and digital engineering areas. Please see https://www.ne.ncsu.edu/ for more information on the organizational unit. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Nuclear Engineering at North Carolina State University invites applications for a 9-month, tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor rank, beginning August 2027. We welcome candidates whose expertise advances nuclear engineering in areas such as advanced reactor design, thermohydraulics, and materials, as well as emerging interdisciplinary fields. As a faculty member, you will help advance nuclear technologies to meet growing energy needs while strengthening the department’s experimental and computational research capabilities. Your work may span next-generation reactor systems, nuclear materials, intelligent energy systems, or the intersections of nuclear technology with digital engineering, infrastructure investment, climate change mitigation, and community engagement. Through research, teaching, and mentorship, you will contribute to the future of nuclear energy and the engineers who will shape it. Key Responsibilities: Advance research and scholarship in the department’s focus areas or emerging fields that complement its strengths. Build a sustainable research program by developing proposals and securing external funding. Disseminate research findings through peer-reviewed publications and technical presentations. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses, including Introduction to Nuclear Engineering and senior design projects. Develop graduate courses that reflect your research expertise and emerging developments in nuclear engineering. Mentor and supervise MS and PhD students conducting research in related fields. Foster experimental, computational, and interdisciplinary collaborations that expand the department’s research capabilities. Bring your expertise, collaborative approach, and commitment to teaching and mentorship to NC State. Other Responsibilities In addition to the core responsibilities of this role, there will be occasional opportunities to take on additional duties. This offers an opportunity to build on your skills, explore new areas, and gain a deeper understanding of the department’s operations. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience PhD in Nuclear Engineering or closely related field and a minimum of 2 years academic (post doc/research scholar/faculty) or national lab or industry experience. Other Required Qualifications Familiarity and computational and/or experimental research experience in nuclear science and engineering, including advanced nuclear systems, thermohydraulics, nuclear materials, plasma science and engineering, radiological and waste engineering, or health physics. Knowledge of or experience applying high technology or digital engineering to nuclear science and engineering, such as advanced modeling and simulation, quantum computing, intelligent nuclear energy systems, machine learning, or artificial intelligence. Proven ability to conduct and disseminate scholarly research through peer-reviewed publications and technical presentations. Preferred Qualifications Experience conducting research across disciplines, including areas such as nuclear technology, energy infrastructure, climate change mitigation, or community engagement, and preparing research proposals to secure external funding. Demonstrated ability to contribute to or lead research within interdisciplinary teams and strengthen experimental and computational research capabilities. Evidence of teaching, training, advising, or mentoring students Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 10/13/2026 Anticipated Close Date 11/15/2026, if posting is active we are still accepting and reviewing applications Special Instructions to Applicants In addition to your application please submit: 1. Cover Letter 2. Resume/CV 3. Contact information for at least three references. 4. Research Statement 5. Teaching Statement Position Details Position Number 00000682 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.00 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 141101 - Nuclear Engineering EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Contact Information for References Research Statement Teaching Statement Resume/CV Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
