    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236755": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of the Practice",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant Professor of the Practice Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant Professor of the Practice Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In addition to your application, please submit the following: 1. Cover Letter 2. Curriculum Vitae 3. Contact Information for References (At least three professional references) 4. Research Statement (Please include both Consulting and Research experience) 5. Teaching Statement Three confidential letters of recommendation will be requested for all finalists. Review of applications will begin 12/1/2026 . Please direct any questions about this position to statisticshr@ncsu.edu. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194996EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant Professor of the Practice Anticipated Hiring Range $80,000 - $90,000 Work Schedule Core Business Hours: Monday - Friday; 8:00 AM - 5:00 PM; Hours are flexible and will vary based on teaching schedule and research needs. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Statistics About the Department The Department of Statistics at North Carolina State University was founded in 1941 by Gertrude M. Cox and is one of the oldest and largest statistics programs in the country. The primary function of the Department is to achieve outstanding research, teaching, mentoring, consulting and collaborations on campus and world-wide, within a cohesive department, where all students, faculty, and staff receive fair treatment. The Department has approximately 40 faculty members, along with more than 260 undergraduate and 150 graduate students. We are the “birthplace” of SAS Institute, the world’s largest privately-owned software company, and one which specializes in statistical applications. The Department maintains a close relationship with SAS and other industry partners through student programs and activities. The Department has expertise in a number of research areas (see https://statistics.sciences.ncsu.edu/research/research-areas/ ). Our graduate program, which is the top producer of statistics PhDs, is nationally recognized for graduate education and research, ranking #18 nationally in US News and World Reports (see https://statistics.sciences.ncsu.edu/know-us/rankings-awards-stats/ ); we also have a thriving online master’s program with approximately 100 students. NC State promotes an integrated approach to problem solving that transforms lives and provides leadership for social, economic, and technological development across North Carolina and around the world. NC State’s land grant mission of teaching, research and service is dedicated to the service of North Carolina and its people. Applicants are encouraged to review the institution’s mission, vision and strategic plan, and consider how their background, interest and experience would enable them to support the university. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Statistics at North Carolina State University in Raleigh, North Carolina, invites applications for a nine-month Assistant Professor of the Practice position (non-tenure track). We are particularly interested in scholars who will develop a robust collaborative statistical program and offer a broad range of instruction for statistics majors and non-majors in fields including machine learning and artificial intelligence. Key Responsibilities Collaborate with researchers at NC State and beyond to establish, develop and sustain externally-funded research that advances applied disciplines. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in statistics and related fields, and serve as the statistical advisor to and committee member for doctoral students in other disciplines for their research, dissertation development, and completion. Collaborate across disciplines, primarily at NC State, to address complex new research through statistical and data science approaches, while contributing to the department’s academic mission and professional and university service. Other Responsibilities Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Ph.D. in Statistics, Biostatistics, Data Science, or related field by the time of employment. Other Required Qualifications Research expertise in statistics or a related field, with relevance to collaborative statistical work. Demonstrated potential to develop a sustained collaborative research program and contribute to peer-reviewed scholarship. Proven ability to teach statistics effectively to statistics majors and non-majors. Preferred Qualifications N/A Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 10/29/2026 Anticipated Close Date 12/18/2026: if posting is still active we are accepting and reviewing applications. Special Instructions to Applicants In addition to your application, please submit the following: 1. Cover Letter 2. Curriculum Vitae 3. Contact Information for References (At least three professional references) 4. Research Statement (Please include both Consulting and Research experience) 5. Teaching Statement Three confidential letters of recommendation will be requested for all finalists. Review of applications will begin 12/1/2026 . Please direct any questions about this position to statisticshr@ncsu.edu. Position Details Position Number 00112402 Position Type Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 178501 - Statistics EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for References Research Statement Teaching Statement Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
