    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236741": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Scholar",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach a Cover Letter, resume/CV, and contact information for three (3) professional references. Please make sure that the information entered on the application matches what is on your resume. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191780PD Position Number 00112367 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 118101 - Biological And Agricultural Engineering Department 118101 - Biological And Agricultural Engineering Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties We are seeking a highly motivated and qualified Postdoctoral Research Associate to contribute to a cooperative research project measuring greenhouse gas ( GHG ) emissions from confined swine production systems in the southeastern United States. The position will be mentored by Lead PI Dr. Mahmoud Sharara and Co-PI Dr. Sanjay Shah (NC State University) in collaboration with national collaborators. This multi-year project will quantify baseline emissions of ammonia (NH3), methane (CH4), and nitrous oxide (N2O) swine farms across North Carolina, spanning all phases of animal growth, and will evaluate advanced manure processing technologies that could reduce emissions. The successful candidate will play a central role in field data collection using open-path Fourier Transform Infrared spectrophotometry (OP- FTIR ) equipment, inverse dispersion modeling (WindTrax), manure and feed sampling, and the development of emission factors and prediction tools. This position is ideal for a candidate interested in building expertise in field-based environmental monitoring, atmospheric emissions modeling, and applied animal agriculture research, with opportunities for leadership in project coordination and mentoring. North Carolina State University is a Research 1, land-grant university, one of three major research universities in the vigorous, multi-sector Research Triangle, with strong programs in agricultural & biological engineering, animal waste management, and environmental science. Duties and Responsibilities: Plan, coordinate, and conduct GHG emissions monitoring campaigns (targeting 14 days per 60-day period, or 21 days per season) across eight to ten cooperating swine farms in North Carolina (10% of position time) Operate, calibrate, and maintain open-path FTIR spectrophotometry equipment and associated meteorological sensors (temperature, relative humidity, rainfall, ultrasonic anemometers at 10-meter elevation) (10% of position time) Apply inverse dispersion modeling (WindTrax) to 15-minute concentration and climatic data to estimate emission fluxes of CH4, NH3, and N2O from lagoons, sprayfields, and naturally-ventilated barns (10% of position time) Coordinate rotation of monitoring equipment across sites and manage logistics with cooperating farms, sponsors, and collaborating USDA - ARS scientists (10% of position time) Collect and coordinate submission of manure and feed samples for external laboratory analysis (pH, electrical conductivity, total solids, volatile solids, nitrogen, sulfur, and carbon concentrations) (5% of position time) Deploy and maintain continuous on-site sensors for temperature and pH monitoring of manure storage structures (lagoons) (5% of position time) Track farm-level data, including animal stocking and removal dates and head counts, to support development of emission factors and prediction tools (10% of position time) Manage, process, and analyze large environmental and lab datasets; support development of methodologies and models for estimating GHG emissions from swine operations (20% of position time) Assist in hiring, training, and supervising field student staff supporting data collection (5% of position time) Publish research findings in peer-reviewed journals and present results at scientific conferences and stakeholder meetings (10% of position time) Mentor students involved in the project (5% of position time) Other Work/Responsibilities Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday – Friday, 8 am-5 pm Department Required Skills Ph.D. in Biological and Agricultural Engineering, Environmental Engineering, Atmospheric Science, Animal Science, or a closely related field. Strong background in air quality/emissions monitoring; environmental instrumentation; experience with GHG monitoring instrumentation is highly desirable. Familiarity with confined animal feeding operations (CAFOs), manure management systems, or agricultural waste treatment technologies. Proficiency in data processing, statistical analysis, and programming (e.g., Python, R, or MATLAB ). Willingness and ability to travel regularly to farm sites across North Carolina and perform outdoor fieldwork in varying weather conditions. Valid driver’s license and ability to operate a field vehicle; ability to lift and transport field equipment. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively within an interdisciplinary, multi-institutional team. Demonstrated track record of scholarly publications in peer-reviewed journals. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Valid NC driver’s license Required License or Certification n/a Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $65,000-$70,000 If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 10/28/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/235684 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Contact Information for References Resume/CV Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236936": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Scholar",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191803PD Position Number 00112431 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 141101 - Nuclear Engineering Department 141101 - Nuclear Engineering Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties The Computational Plasma Science Group in the Nuclear Engineering Department at North Carolina State University is seeking a postdoctoral research scholar. The postdoctoral researcher will be responsible for plasma and electromagnetic modeling of high powered inductively coupled hydrogen plasmas.The computational modeling will support the development of a low temperature plasma source which produces ions for the neutral beam injectors on a DIII -D tokamak. The project will involve collaboration with experimentalists working on reduced-scale andfull-scale test setups for model validation and to provide physics insights to inform key design decisions. The findings should be published in peer-reviewed journals. The postdoctoral research scholar will work closely with Dr. Amanda Lietz and in collaboration with an experimental team including Dr. Florian Laggner and Dr.Steven Shannon. The ideal candidate should be capable of taking on a leadership role in planned research, execute the research in a timely manner, and deliver milestones. Other Work/Responsibilities Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 9am - 5pm Department Required Skills Ph.D. Degree in the field of Nuclear Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Physics or related field. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Knowledge of plasma physics, inductively coupled plasmas.Strong written and oral communication skills Experience using high performance computing Experience with C++ and Fortran Required License or Certification n/a Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $70,000 - $75,000 If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 10/30/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236924 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? (Open Ended Question) If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Contact Information for References Resume/CV Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
