    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/236928": {
      "title": "Onsite Wastewater Specialist",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Onsite Wastewater Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Onsite Wastewater Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. As a part of your application please attach the following: 1. Cover Letter 2. Resume/CV 3. Extension Statement (other document 1) - 2 pages max 4. Contact information for three (3) professional references. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG195004EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Onsite Wastewater Specialist Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with Experience ($75,000 – $85,000) Work Schedule Monday-Friday, 8AM-5PM Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Crop and Soil Sciences About the Department The Department of Crop and Soil Sciences encompasses diverse disciplines in research, extension, and teaching. The department’s mission is to develop future leaders in crop, soil, and environmental sciences, improve crop plants and products, devise effective and sustainable crop production systems, devise effective and sustainable soil management techniques in both agricultural and urban settings; and disseminate crop, soil, and environmental science knowledge for the benefit of users and producers of food, feed, turf, biofuels, and fiber in North Carolina, the nation, and the world. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Extension Assistant Professor for On-site Wastewater Management leads the Department of Crop and Soil Sciences’ statewide Extension training program that prepares on-site wastewater professionals for certification and keeps certified professionals current through continuing education. Through hands-on schools and workshops at the Lake Wheeler Field Laboratory in Raleigh and other training locations across the state, along with the annual NC Onsite Treatment Conference, this position trains septic system installers, inspectors, operators, local health department staff, and Extension agents from every region of North Carolina. The program also covers the safe land application of biosolids and other organic wastes. Every person trained helps ensure that wastewater from homes, businesses, and communities is treated properly, protecting public health, drinking water sources, and the streams, rivers, and coastal waters that North Carolinians depend on. Extension Program Delivery and Training: Plan, schedule, and teach certification schools, workshops, and continuing education courses for on-site wastewater professionals, local health department personnel, Extension agents, and other stakeholders, primarily at the Lake Wheeler Field Laboratory with additional sessions offered across the state. Deliver instruction on on-site wastewater system design, installation, operation, and maintenance, and on the land application of municipal wastewater residuals (biosolids) and other organic wastes. Assist in organizing the annual NC Onsite Treatment Conference by helping develop the program agenda, recruiting speakers, coordinating logistics with the planning team, and presenting educational sessions. Evaluate the effectiveness of training programs using participant surveys and learning assessments, and use the results to improve course content and delivery. Curriculum and Educational Resource Development: Develop and update training curricula, training manuals, and course materials so content reflects current North Carolina regulations, technologies, and industry practices. Write and publish fact sheets, Extension bulletins, technical publications, and reports on on-site wastewater treatment and land application of residuals for professional and public audiences. Training Facilities and Demonstration Management : Develop, maintain, and improve hands-on training facilities and demonstration systems at the Lake Wheeler Field Laboratory (Raleigh) and the Mountain Horticultural Crops Extension Center (Mills River). Maintain wastewater and land application training displays and equipment; inspect them before training events and arrange repairs and upgrades so demonstrations remain functional and up to date. Partnerships and Stakeholder Engagement: Build and maintain partnerships with industry, government agencies, local health departments, professional organizations, and other stakeholders; for example, meet with regulatory and industry partners to identify training needs and co-sponsor educational events. Other Responsibilities Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience A Ph.D. in Soil Science, Agronomy, Agricultural Education, Biological Engineering, Agricultural Engineering, Environmental Engineering, or a closely related field is required Other Required Qualifications Excellent written and oral communication skills and the ability to teach and communicate effectively with adult learners. Ability to develop, deliver, and evaluate applied, hands-on training programs and to work effectively with Extension personnel, government agencies, industry, and other stakeholders. Knowledge of on-site wastewater treatment systems and irrigation systems, and the soils of North Carolina and their relationship with on-site wastewater treatment systems. Writing skills necessary for producing programmatic output, including reports, Extension bulletins, fact sheets, and training materials and manuals. Preferred Qualifications Experience in on-site wastewater management, land application of wastewater residuals, or a related field. Previous work with health departments, an agronomic or soil science background, knowledge of on-site wastewater treatment and disposal systems, and the ability to troubleshoot system-related problems. Demonstrated ability to deliver professional training or Extension programs, educational material development, and hands-on or mechanical work is also desirable. Familiarity with NC-specific regulatory bodies and stakeholder networks relevant to on-site wastewater treatment, e.g., local health departments and professional associations related to the area. Required License(s) or Certification(s) A valid NC Driver’s License or the ability to obtain an NC Driver’s License within 60 days of hire. A valid Driver’s License must be maintained throughout employment Valid NC Driver's License required Yes Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 10/30/2026 Anticipated Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants As a part of your application please attach the following: 1. Cover Letter 2. Resume/CV 3. Extension Statement (other document 1) – 2 pages max 4. Contact information for three (3) professional references. Position Details Position Number 00112420 Position Type Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.00 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 110901 - Crop and Soil Sciences EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * A valid driver's license is required. This license must be maintained throughout employment. Do you have a valid driver's license and the ability to obtain a North Carolina Driver's License within 60 days of hire? Yes No * Do you have or will have by the start date a Ph.D. in Soil Science, Agronomy, Agricultural Education, Biological Engineering, Agricultural Engineering, or Environmental Engineering, or a closely related field? Yes No * Do you have knowledge of on-site wastewater treatment systems and irrigation systems? Yes No Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Other Document (1) Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
